B.awo=s(["al-kahf","kahf"],t.s)
B.bqf=new A.K(B.awo,"Surah Al-Kahf (18) is the surah many Muslims recite on Fridays, and memorising its opening verses is a widely taught practice. Open the Qur'an screen to read it, or ask a teacher about its virtues so that they can show you the sources.")
B.aOj=s(["anxiety","anxious","worry","worried","stress","stressed","grief","dua for anxiety","dua for worry","dua for stress"],t.s)
B.bqp=new A.K(B.aOj,"\u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f\u0645\u064e\u0651 \u0625\u0650\u0646\u0650\u0651\u064a \u0623\u064e\u0639\u064f\u0648\u0630\u064f \u0628\u0650\u0643\u064e \u0645\u0650\u0646\u064e \u0627\u0644\u0652\u0647\u064e\u0645\u0650\u0651 \u0648\u064e\u0627\u0644\u0652\u062d\u064e\u0632\u064e\u0646\u0650 \u2014 \u201cO Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, from incapacity and laziness, from cowardice and miserliness, from the burden of debt and from being overpowered by men.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 6369). You will also find it in your Morning Adhkar set.")
B.aLj=s(["witr","pray witr","how do i pray witr","how to pray witr"],t.s)
B.bqr=new A.K(B.aLj,"Witr is prayed after \u2018Isha until Fajr, as an odd number of rak'ahs \u2014 most simply one: the night prayer is two by two, and if dawn is near, one rak'ah makes it witr (Sahih al-Bukhari 990). The Prophet \ufdfa said Allah is single (witr) and loves what is single, and told the people of the Qur'an to pray witr (Sunan Abi Dawud 1416, sahih per al-Albani). He also taught al-Hasan ibn Ali a Qunut supplication for Witr that begins \u201cAllahumma ihdini fiman hadayt\u2026\u201d (Sunan Abi Dawud 1425, sahih per al-Albani). That report does not say whether it is said before or after ruku\u2018: ask a scholar of your madhhab.")
B.aFX=s(["morning adhkar","adhkar","dhikr","remembrance"],t.s)
B.bs2=new A.K(B.aFX,"Your Dhikr & Du'a screen holds the morning, evening, and after-prayer sets from Hisn al-Muslim with meanings. One report: whoever says a short \u201cIn the name of Allah\u2026\u201d formula three times in the morning is protected from sudden calamity until evening, and three times in the evening until morning (Sunan Abi Dawud 5088, sahih per al-Albani). Open it from Home and tap the counters as you recite.")
B.aGC=s(["ramadan","fasting","fast","sawm","siyam","roza","suhoor","iftar","ramadhan","ramzan","ramazan"],t.s)
B.boJ=new A.K(B.aGC,"Fasting Ramadan is the fourth pillar of Islam (Qur'an 2:183-185). \u201cWhoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and hope for reward, his past sins are forgiven.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 38). Take suhoor \u2014 \u201cin suhoor there is blessing\u201d (Bukhari 1923) \u2014 and check the Islamic Calendar screen for this year's dates.")
B.aON=s(["zakat","charity","sadaqah","almsgiving"],t.s)
B.brf=new A.K(B.aON,"Zakat is the third pillar \u2014 2.5% of qualifying wealth held a lunar year above the nisab. The Prophet \ufdfa told Mu'adh, when sending him to Yemen, that Allah has made charity obligatory on their wealth, taken from the rich and given to the poor (Sahih al-Bukhari 1395). The Zakat screen in Ar-Rayaan calculates it for you step by step.")
B.aE5=s(["prayer time","prayer times","salah times","namaz time"],t.s)
B.bpg=new A.K(B.aE5,"Your Prayer Times screen calculates today's schedule right on your device \u2014 tap GPS or choose your city, and turn on the bell next to any prayer to be alerted when its time arrives.\n[GO:/prayer]")
B.aCp=s(["how do i pray","how to pray","salah","salaat","salat","namaz","two rakah","pray two","pray 2","namaz ka tareeqa","namaz ka tariqa","namaz kaise","method of prayer","how to perform salah","steps of prayer"],t.s)
B.bps=new A.K(B.aCp,"Prayer is the second pillar. \u201cPray as you have seen me pray.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 631). Five daily prayers are obligatory. A two-rak'ah prayer, in outline: make the intention, face the qibla and say Allahu Akbar, recite al-Fatihah and a surah, bow (ruku'), rise, prostrate (sujud), sit briefly and prostrate again. Stand for the second rak'ah and repeat it, then sit for the tashahhud and finish with the salam to the right and the left. Small details differ between the schools, so learn them from a teacher. The Huda guides in this app go step by step, and Shaykh Saqib Iqbal's channel (in Our Sources) teaches it beautifully.\n[GO:/huda]")
B.aE0=s(["quran","qur'an","koran","recite","recitation"],t.s)
B.brR=new A.K(B.aE0,"The Qur'an screen holds all 114 surahs \u2014 tap any ayah to hear recitation by Shaykh Mishary Rashid Alafasy. \u201cThe best of you are those who learn the Qur'an and teach it.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 5027).")
B.aJ8=s(["du'a","dua","supplication"],t.s)
B.brG=new A.K(B.aJ8,"Du'a is worship itself (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3372, sahih per Darussalam). For a need, begin with praise of Allah and salawat on the Prophet \ufdfa, then ask with certainty. Your Dhikr & Du'a screen carries the authentic daily supplications with their meanings.")
B.aG1=s(["eid"],t.s)
B.boH=new A.K(B.aG1,"The two Eids are days of prayer, takbir, and celebration (Sahih al-Bukhari 950-956). Eid al-Fitr follows Ramadan; Eid al-Adha falls on 10 Dhul-Hijjah, the day after Arafah. Exact dates for this year are on the Islamic Calendar screen.")
B.axf=s(["sources","authentic","hadith book","sihah","bukhari"],t.s)
B.bqQ=new A.K(B.axf,"Ar-Rayaan builds only on the Qur'an and the Sihah Sitta \u2014 the six authentic books: Sahih al-Bukhari, Sahih Muslim, Sunan Abu Dawood, Jami' at-Tirmidhi, Sunan an-Nasa'i, and Sunan Ibn Majah \u2014 with Shaykh Muhammad Saqib Iqbal's channel for guided learning. See the full list on the Our Sources screen.")
B.aHI=s(["hajj","pilgrimage"],t.s)
B.bqE=new A.K(B.aHI,"Hajj is the fifth pillar, owed once in a lifetime by those able (Qur'an 3:97). \u201cAn accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 1773). Umrah can be performed any time of year.")
B.aOu=s(["tahajjud","night prayer","qiyam"],t.s)
B.bqo=new A.K(B.aOu,"The night prayer is the best prayer after the obligatory ones (Sahih Muslim 1163). The last third of the night is a special time for du'a \u2014 your Prayer Times screen shows tonight's window.")
B.avm=s(["forgive","repent","tawbah","sin","same sin","keep sinning","sin again","sinning again","repeated sin","fall into sin","sin over and over"],t.s)
B.bs0=new A.K(B.avm,"Allah says: \u201cdo not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins.\u201d (Qur'an 39:53). The Prophet \ufdfa said: \u201cEvery son of Adam sins, and the best of sinners are those who repent.\u201d (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 2499, weak per Darussalam). The door is open \u2014 walk through it.")
B.aK3=s(["mother","father","parents"],t.s)
B.brk=new A.K(B.aK3,"A man asked to go out and fight; the Prophet \ufdfa said: \u201cThen stay with her, for Paradise is beneath her feet.\u201d (Sunan an-Nasa'i 3104, sahih per Darussalam). The Prophet \ufdfa was asked who most deserves good companionship: \u201cYour mother\u201d \u2014 three times \u2014 \u201cthen your father.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 5971).")
B.aId=s(["istighfar","sayyid"],t.s)
B.boh=new A.K(B.aId,"Sayyid al-Istighfar is the master supplication for forgiveness \u2014 it opens your Morning Adhkar set. Whoever says it with conviction in the morning and dies that day enters Paradise (Sahih al-Bukhari 6306).")
B.aOa=s(["patience","sabr","hardship","difficult","trial","patience in the quran","patience in quran","what does allah say about patience"],t.s)
B.bqn=new A.K(B.aOa,"\u201cIndeed, Allah is with the patient.\u201d (Qur'an 2:153). \u201cAmazing is the affair of the believer: all of it is good for him \u2014 gratitude in ease, patience in hardship.\u201d (Sahih Muslim 2999). This too shall pass, and nothing is wasted with Him.")
B.aFQ=s(["name of allah","names of allah","99"],t.s)
B.bru=new A.K(B.aFQ,"\u201cAllah has ninety-nine names; whoever preserves them enters Paradise.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 2736). Begin with Ar-Rahman \u2014 the Most Merciful \u2014 the name He opens His Book with.")
B.aD3=s(["salaam","salam","assalamu","wa alaikum"],t.s)
B.boo=new A.K(B.aD3,"Wa alaikum as-salam wa rahmatullah - and upon you be peace and mercy. How may I walk beside you today? Ask me about worship, the Qur'an, this app, or simply talk.")
B.aEg=s(["how are you","how do you feel"],t.s)
B.bsg=new A.K(B.aEg,"Alhamdulillah - all praise belongs to Allah. More importantly: how are YOU? If something weighs on your heart, I can make du'a with you, or take you to Sakina for stillness.")
B.aq8=s(["who are you","your name","your hadi"],t.s)
B.bmX=new A.K(B.aq8,"I am Hadi - \"the guide\" - your companion inside Ar-Rayaan. I answer from the Qur'an and the Sihah Sitta: Sahih al-Bukhari, Sahih Muslim, Sunan Abu Dawood, Jami' at-Tirmidhi, Sunan an-Nasa'i, and Sunan Ibn Majah - and I know every room of this app. I would rather say \"I don't know\" than invent. My sister-teacher Wasia runs the letter school.")
B.aKJ=s(["who is wasia","what is wasia"],t.s)
B.bro=new A.K(B.aKJ,"Wasia is the AI teacher of the Wasia Academy - the letter school built with love. She teaches the Arabic alphabet, reads with the child, and speaks in three voices: student, parent, and a Teachers' Corner for parents. Shall I take you there?\n[GO:/academy/gate]")
B.aML=s(["thank","jazak","shukran","thanks"],t.s)
B.bpQ=new A.K(B.aML,"Wa iyyakum - and you likewise, many times over. May Allah accept from you. I am here whenever you need me.")
B.ay3=s(["what can you do","what do you do","features","guide me"],t.s)
B.bqC=new A.K(B.ay3,"Three things, always: (1) answer from the Qur'an and the Sihah Sitta - verses, du'as, rulings, with sources; (2) teach you this app room by room - prayer times, Qur'an, stories, zakat, games; (3) walk you there myself - just say \"take me to...\" and I will. What shall we begin with?")
B.aIU=s(["quran screen","read the quran","recitation screen","open quran"],t.s)
B.bpf=new A.K(B.aIU,"Here is the Qur'an - tap any ayah to hear Shaykh Mishary Rashid Alafasy recite.\n[GO:/quran]")
B.aJE=s(["prayer times screen","prayer screen","salah times screen"],t.s)
B.bpP=new A.K(B.aJE,"Here is your Prayer Times - tap the bell beside any prayer to be alerted when its time arrives.\n[GO:/prayer]")
B.aD7=s(["adhkar screen","dhikr screen","dua screen","du'a screen"],t.s)
B.bmu=new A.K(B.aD7,"Here is Dhikr & Du'a - the Hisn al-Muslim sets with counters and meanings.\n[GO:/adhkar]")
B.ar7=s(["zakat screen","zakat calculator"],t.s)
B.br0=new A.K(B.ar7,"Here is the Zakat calculator - it walks you through nisab and rates step by step.\n[GO:/zakat]")
B.av0=s(["stories screen","story screen","prophets screen"],t.s)
B.bpH=new A.K(B.av0,"Here is Stories - Prophets, Women, Seerah, Companions, duas and khutbahs. Inside any story you can ask me about it as you read.\n[GO:/stories]")
B.ax_=s(["search screen","find anything","find screen"],t.s)
B.bnK=new A.K(B.ax_,"Here is Find Anything - one search across every shelf of the app.\n[GO:/search]")
B.aGD=s(["games screen","game screen"],t.s)
B.bso=new A.K(B.aGD,"Here is Games - Shatranj, Ludo, Trivia, and the 99 Names.\n[GO:/games]")
B.awD=s(["99 names screen","names screen","names of allah screen"],t.s)
B.brJ=new A.K(B.awD,'Here is the 99 Names - learn them one by one; "whoever preserves them enters Paradise."\n[GO:/games/names99]')
B.axZ=s(["hadith screen","forty hadith","nawawi screen"],t.s)
B.bpD=new A.K(B.axZ,"Here is the Forty Hadith of an-Nawawi, Arabic with meanings.\n[GO:/hadith]")
B.aqf=s(["qibla screen","find qibla","qibla direction","face qibla"],t.s)
B.bno=new A.K(B.aqf,"Here is Qibla - hold your phone flat and it points you to the Ka'bah.\n[GO:/qibla]")
B.aLi=s(["calendar screen","islamic calendar","ramadan dates","eid dates"],t.s)
B.boM=new A.K(B.aLi,"Here is the Islamic Calendar - this year's months, Ramadan and Eid dates.\n[GO:/calendar]")
B.aKh=s(["finance screen","stocks screen","trading screen","halal stocks"],t.s)
B.bnn=new A.K(B.aKh,"Here is Tayyib Finance - the halal stock screener and a paper trading floor to practice on.\n[GO:/finance]")
B.aO6=s(["academy screen","school screen","letters screen","alphabet"],t.s)
B.bnF=new A.K(B.aO6,"Here is Wasia Academy - where children learn the Arabic letters with Wasia.\n[GO:/academy/gate]")
B.aHV=s(["feelings screen","heart screen"],t.s)
B.bmz=new A.K(B.aHV,"Here is For Your Heart - a gentle feelings guide with a du'a for every state.\n[GO:/feelings]")
B.aFL=s(["sakina","comfort screen","peace screen"],t.s)
B.bpT=new A.K(B.aFL,"Here is Sakina - a page of stillness for when the heart is heavy.\n[GO:/sakina]")
B.atC=s(["family tree screen","messengers screen"],t.s)
B.bmv=new A.K(B.atC,"Here is the Messengers' family tree - from Adam to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon them all).\n[GO:/family-tree]")
B.aDJ=s(["share screen","cards screen","verse cards"],t.s)
B.brr=new A.K(B.aDJ,"Here is verse cards - share an ayah with someone you love.\n[GO:/share]")
B.apN=s(["sources screen","our sources"],t.s)
B.bqA=new A.K(B.apN,"Here is Our Sources - every authority this app builds on.\n[GO:/sources]")
B.awa=s(["settings screen","api key","apikey","add a key"],t.s)
B.bqX=new A.K(B.awa,"Here is Settings - in Hadi's section you can add your free API key so I can reason further; without one I still answer from the curated shelf.\n[GO:/settings]")
B.avi=s(["masajid","masjid","mosque","halal food","restaurants"],t.s)
B.bog=new A.K(B.avi,"Here is Masajid & Halal - prayer spaces and halal food near you.\n[GO:/masajid]")
B.aJG=s(["shahada","shahadah","kalima","testimony","declaration of faith"],t.s)
B.bp_=new A.K(B.aJG,'The testimony: "La ilaha illallah, Muhammadur rasulullah" - there is no god worthy of worship but Allah, and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. The first pillar; on it everything stands.')
B.avS=s(["pillars of islam","five pillars"],t.s)
B.bqx=new A.K(B.avS,"The five pillars: the testimony of faith, the five daily prayers, zakat, the fast of Ramadan, and Hajj for those able - each established in the Qur'an and the Sunnah.")
B.aNM=s(["wudu","ablution","wuzu","wudoo"],t.s)
B.bse=new A.K(B.aNM,'Wudu is the purification before prayer: wash the face, hands to the elbows, wipe head and ears, wash the feet - with intention and in order. "Allah does not accept prayer without purification." (Sahih Muslim 224).')
B.aok=s(["grave","after death","hereafter"],t.s)
B.bqS=new A.K(B.aok,'The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: "Remember often the destroyer of pleasures - death." (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 2307, hasan per Darussalam). Live each prayer as if it were your last; the grave is a garden from Paradise or a pit from the Fire - and its morning is near.')
B.aJi=s(["morning adhkar","evening adhkar","morning dua","evening dua","morning remembrance","evening remembrance"],t.s)
B.bnI=new A.K(B.aJi,'The morning and evening adhkar are the shield of the day: Ayat al-Kursi, the three Quls, "Raditu billahi rabba..." - whoever says them morning and evening is sufficed. They live in your Dhikr & Du\'a sets with counters and meanings.')
B.aBu=s(["before eating","after eating","eating dua","food dua","eat dua"],t.s)
B.bn2=new A.K(B.aBu,'Before eating: "Bismillah" - and if you forget at the start, say "Bismillahi awwalahu wa akhirahu" (Sunan Abi Dawud 3767, sahih per al-Albani). After eating, the Prophet \ufdfa is reported to have said: "Alhamdulillahilladhi at\'amana wa saqana wa ja\'alana muslimin" - all praise to Allah who fed us, gave us drink, and made us Muslims (Sunan Abi Dawud 3850; sunnah.com shows al-Albani\'s grade as da\'if (weak), so hold it as a reported wording, not a firm Sunnah).')
B.axe=s(["dua for parents","my parents","parents","mother dua","father dua"],t.s)
B.bmw=new A.K(B.axe,"The Qur'an itself teaches the du'a: \"Rabbir hamhumaa kamaa rabbayaani saghira\" - My Lord, have mercy on them as they raised me when I was small (Al-Isra 24). Say it after every prayer; it is among the most beloved of speech.")
B.aH1=s(["dua for the sick","someone sick","visiting the sick","ill dua","cure dua"],t.s)
B.bpe=new A.K(B.aH1,'For pain: place your hand on the spot that hurts, say "Bismillah" three times, then seven times seek refuge in Allah and His power from the harm you feel and fear (Sahih Muslim 2202). When visiting a sick person whose time has not yet come, say seven times a supplication asking Allah the Mighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to cure him (Sunan Abi Dawud 3106, sahih per al-Albani). The one who visits a sick person is, in the Prophet\'s words, in the fruit garden of Paradise until he returns (Sahih Muslim 2568).')
B.ayd=s(["anxious","anxiety","worried","worry","depressed","overwhelmed","scared","afraid"],t.s)
B.bqI=new A.K(B.ayd,'For a heavy heart: "Hasbunallahu wa ni\'mal wakeel" - Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best Disposer of affairs (Al-Imran 173) - the words of Ibrahim and our Prophet in distress. And when something distressed him, the Prophet (peace be upon him) would say: "Ya Hayyu ya Qayyum, bi-rahmatika astagheeth." (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 3524, hasan per Darussalam). Sakina is in this app for you too.')
B.aBv=s(["niyyah","intention","why do we","actions are"],t.s)
B.boz=new A.K(B.aBv,'"Actions are only by intentions, and every person shall have what he intended." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1 - the very first hadith). The reward of an act lives in its intention: prayer for showing off is empty, and sweeping a floor for Allah is worship.')
B.au8=s(["mercy","be kind","kindness","gentle","compassion"],t.s)
B.bnp=new A.K(B.au8,'"The merciful are shown mercy by Ar-Rahman. Be merciful to those on earth, and the One above the heavens will be merciful to you." (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 1924, hasan per Darussalam). "He who does not show mercy will not be shown mercy." (Sahih al-Bukhari 6013). Kindness - rifq - beautifies everything it touches.')
B.aFZ=s(["neighbor","neighbour","next door"],t.s)
B.brj=new A.K(B.aFZ,"Jibreel kept advising the Prophet about the neighbor until he thought he would make him an heir: the neighbor has a right almost of kinship. (Sahih al-Bukhari 6015) Good neighborhood - guarding dignity, sharing food, soft greetings - is faith in daily dress.")
B.ayM=s(["gossip","backbite","speak good","talk bad","rumors"],t.s)
B.brZ=new A.K(B.ayM,'"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent." (Sahih al-Bukhari 6018). Backbiting - mentioning your brother with what he dislikes - is described in the Qur\'an as eating the flesh of a dead brother (Al-Hujurat 12). If speech is not good, silence is worship.')
B.aIA=s(["sadaqah","charity","give money","donate"],t.s)
B.bpR=new A.K(B.aIA,'"Charity does not decrease wealth." (Sahih Muslim 2588). "Your smile in your brother\'s face is charity; removing harm from the path is charity." (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 1956, hasan per Darussalam). The zakat calculator in this app handles the obligatory share; beyond it, "protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date" (Sahih al-Bukhari 1417).')
B.aBi=s(["tawbah","repent","repentance","forgiveness","forgive me","sinned"],t.s)
B.bpG=new A.K(B.aBi,'Allah says: "do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins." (Az-Zumar 53). The Prophet said: "By the One in Whose hand is my soul, if you did not sin, Allah would replace you with people who sin and seek forgiveness - and He would forgive them." (Sahih Muslim 2749). Repentance: leave the sin, regret it, resolve not to return - and restore rights if anyone was wronged.')
B.aA6=s(["hajj","pilgrimage","makkah trip"],t.s)
B.bqD=new A.K(B.aA6,'Hajj, the fifth pillar, is owed once in a lifetime by whoever can find a way: "And [due] to Allah from the people is a pilgrimage to the House - for whoever is able to find thereto a way" (Al-Imran 97). "An accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1773). Its rites gather at the Ka\'bah, Arafat, Muzdalifah, and Mina across Dhul-Hijjah.')
B.aze=s(["umrah","minor pilgrimage","omra"],t.s)
B.bnw=new A.K(B.aze,"Umrah is the shorter pilgrimage, performable any time of year: ihram, tawaf of the Ka'bah, sa'i between Safa and Marwah, and shaving or shortening the hair. The Prophet \ufdfa told a woman who had missed the Hajj to perform Umrah in Ramadan, because an Umrah in Ramadan carries the reward of Hajj (Sahih al-Bukhari 1782).")
B.aKe=s(["tahajjud","night prayer","qiyam","pray at night"],t.s)
B.bna=new A.K(B.aKe,'"The best prayer after the obligatory prayers is the night prayer." (Sahih Muslim 1163). Tahajjud is prayed after sleeping a portion of the night, in units of two: "They arise from [their] beds; they supplicate their Lord in fear and aspiration" (As-Sajdah 16). Start with two rak\'ah before Fajr; Allah descends to the lowest heaven asking who is calling upon Him. (Bukhari 1145)')
B.aAF=s(["istikhara","decision dua","big decision","choice dua"],t.s)
B.bnB=new A.K(B.aAF,"For any matter - marriage, a job, a move - pray two units of non-obligatory prayer, then the du'a of istikhara taught by the Prophet himself: \"Allahumma inni astakhiruka bi-'ilmik...\" - O Allah, I seek Your choice by Your knowledge... Then go ahead with what you decide and rely on Allah. The Prophet \ufdfa taught the istikhara to his companions as he taught them a surah of the Qur'an, saying: \"If one of you is concerned about a matter, let him pray two rak'ahs other than the obligatory prayer.\" (Sahih al-Bukhari 1166)")
B.aLF=s(["laylatul qadr","night of decree","qadr","best night","odd nights"],t.s)
B.bpx=new A.K(B.aLF,'Laylatul Qadr, in the last ten nights of Ramadan - in the odd nights, the 21st, 23rd, 25th, 27th, 29th: "Better than a thousand months" (Al-Qadr 3). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Search for it in the odd nights of the last ten nights of Ramadan" (Sahih al-Bukhari 2017). So stand, recite, ask. What would you do with 83 years of worship in one night?')
B.av1=s(["breaking fast","iftar dua","iftar","end of fast"],t.s)
B.bn1=new A.K(B.av1,"When breaking the fast, the Prophet \ufdfa said: \"Dhahaba al-zama'u wabtallat al-urooqu wa thabata al-ajru in sha Allah\" - The thirst is gone, the veins are moistened, and the reward is fixed, if Allah wills. (Sunan Abi Dawud 2357, hasan per al-Albani). The fasting person has a du'a at the moment of breaking that is not rejected. (Ibn Majah 1753, hasan per Darussalam)")
B.aEH=s(["durood","salawat","bless the prophet","blessings on the prophet"],t.s)
B.bqz=new A.K(B.aEH,'"Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten upon him." (Sahih Muslim 408). The least of it: "Allahumma salli \'ala Muhammad" - O Allah, send Your peace and blessings upon Muhammad. It is the signature of love: your prayer is not complete without it.')
B.azw=s(["spread salam","say salam","greeting islam","how to greet"],t.s)
B.bmJ=new A.K(B.azw,'The Prophet \ufdfa said you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another - and showed the way: spread the greeting of peace among yourselves (Sahih Muslim 54). Asked which part of Islam is best, he named feeding people and greeting those you know and those you do not (Sahih al-Bukhari 28). The greeting of Islam - "As-salamu alaikum warahmatullah" - carries three levels: peace, then mercy, then Allah\'s blessings.')
B.aCO=s(["seeking knowledge","learn islam","study","ilm","become a scholar"],t.s)
B.bsf=new A.K(B.aCO,'"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim." (Sunan Ibn Majah 224, very weak per Darussalam - the chain is debated, but the meaning is carried by the whole religion). The best of you, said the Prophet, are those who learn the Qur\'an and teach it. (Sahih al-Bukhari 5027). Ten minutes daily outlasts a weekend of regret.')
B.awY=s(["plant a tree","small deeds","tiny good deed","good deeds small"],t.s)
B.boP=new A.K(B.awY,'"If a Muslim plants a tree, or sows a crop, and a bird or a person or an animal eats of it, it is counted as charity for him." (Sahih al-Bukhari 2320). And the man who gave a thirsty dog water - Allah accepted the deed and forgave him. (Sahih al-Bukhari 2363) No good deed is too small for His scale.')
B.aLN=s(["names on the day of judgment","resurrection names","called by name","name on judgment day"],t.s)
B.bnX=new A.K(B.aLN,"It is reported that the Prophet said you will be called on the Day of Resurrection by your names and the names of your fathers, so make your names beautiful (Sunan Abi Dawud 4948 - graded da'if (weak) by al-Albani, so held as a weak report only). A reflection, not a hadith: a name carried with goodness becomes a light.")
B.aDo=s(["sick suffering","going through hardship","why me","afflicted","trials"],t.s)
B.bp5=new A.K(B.aDo,'The Prophet said: "When Allah wills good for a slave, He afflicts him." (Sahih al-Bukhari 5645) - and "No fatigue, illness, anxiety, sorrow, harm or sadness touches a Muslim, even a thorn, but Allah expiates by it." (Bukhari 5641). The pain you did not choose becomes the expiation you did not earn.')
B.aKc=s(["leaving home","entering home","go out","come back home","exit the house"],t.s)
B.bsb=new A.K(B.aKc,"Leaving home: \"Bismillahi, tawakkaltu 'alallah, la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah\" - In Allah's name, I trust in Allah; there is no might nor power except with Allah - it is said to you: you are guided, sufficed, and protected. (Sunan Abi Dawud 5095, sahih per al-Albani). Entering home: mention Allah's name as you enter (Sahih Muslim 2018) and give greetings of peace (Qur'an 24:61).")
B.aJ9=s(["travel dua","going on a trip","road trip dua","flying dua","journey dua","travel","trip"],t.s)
B.bsl=new A.K(B.aJ9,'Before and during travel: "Subhanalladhi sakhkhara lana hadha wa ma kunna lahu muqrinin, wa inna ila rabbina lamunqalibun" - Glory to Him who subjected this to us, and we could never have accomplished it ourselves - and indeed, to our Lord we will return. (Sahih Muslim 1342). Shorten the four-unit prayers when you travel beyond the city.')
B.aJH=s(["sneezing","sneeze","alhamdulillah sneeze","bless sneeze"],t.s)
B.brM=new A.K(B.aJH,'When someone sneezes and praises Allah ("Alhamdulillah"), say "Yarhamukumullah" - may Allah have mercy on you. The sneezer replies "Yahdikumullah..." (Sahih al-Bukhari 6224). A learned custom: sneeze in privacy, praise Allah, and be answered with mercy.')
B.as4=s(["dream interpretation","had a dream","strange dream","bad dream","nightmare","dream"],t.s)
B.bpy=new A.K(B.as4,"The Prophet taught: the righteous dream is from Allah; the distressing dream is from shaytan - spit to your left and seek refuge in Allah from its evil, and it will not harm you (Sahih al-Bukhari 3292); the report in Sahih Muslim 2261 says to spit three times. Not every dream carries a meaning - most are what the daytime leaves behind.")
B.aC1=s(["evil eye","hasad","envy","someone envied me","nazr","ruqyah","protect my children"],t.s)
B.bqM=new A.K(B.aC1,"The Prophet \ufdfa said the evil eye is real, that if anything could outrun the decree it would be the evil eye, and that when you are asked to wash for it, you should wash (Sahih Muslim 2188). Many Muslims recite Ayat al-Kursi and the three Quls for protection. For ruqyah, the greatest of it is Al-Fatiha - a Companion once recited it over a tribal chief who had been bitten, and the Prophet approved the payment he accepted. (Bukhari 5736)")
B.aNZ=s(["marriage proposal","getting married","choosing spouse","marry someone","marriage advice","marry","marriage"],t.s)
B.bo8=new A.K(B.aNZ,"The Prophet's counsel: \"When someone whose religion and character pleases you proposes to you, then marry him. If you do not, there will be corruption in the land and widespread evil.\" (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 1085, weak per Darussalam). Religion first - beauty and wealth open like flowers and close like them; faith is the root that stays.")
B.ax5=s(["wedding dua","nikkah dua","just married","newlywed"],t.s)
B.bnQ=new A.K(B.ax5,"The blessed wedding du'a: \"Barakallahu laka wa baraka 'alaika wa jama'a bainakuma fi khayr\" - May Allah bless you, shower blessings upon you, and join you both in goodness. (Sunan Abi Dawud 2130, sahih per al-Albani). A reflection, not a hadith: the house of the newlyweds is built upon five - gratitude, gentleness, patience, honesty, and prayer together.")
B.aB1=s(["new baby","newborn","baby born","child born","aqiqah","tahnik","baby"],t.s)
B.bs7=new A.K(B.aB1,'For the newborn: the Prophet \ufdfa called the adhan in the ear of al-Hasan when he was born (Sunan Abi Dawud 5105, hasan per al-Albani). Tahnik: a softened date on the palate, and pray for the child. (Sahih al-Bukhari 5469). And the aqiqah: "Every child is pledged to its aqiqah" - an animal sacrificed on the seventh day, and the child named. (Tirmidhi 1513, hasan per Darussalam)')
B.avX=s(["children","raising kids","my child","teaching children","kids behavior"],t.s)
B.brz=new A.K(B.avX,'"Every child is born upon the fitrah - the natural readiness for Islam; its parents make it a Jew, a Christian, or a Magian (Zoroastrian)." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1385). Be the first kindness they know: the Prophet carried children, shortened the prayer when he heard a baby cry, and said: "He is not of us who does not have mercy on our young." (Tirmidhi 1919, hasan per Darussalam)')
B.axa=s(["friday","jumuah","jumma","surah kahf","best hour friday"],t.s)
B.brF=new A.K(B.axa,'Friday: purify and adorn, go early to the masjid, and leave trading aside when the call is made - "And when the prayer has been concluded, disperse within the land and seek from the bounty of Allah" (Al-Jumuah 9-10). The Prophet said Friday has an hour in which no Muslim happens to ask Allah for good but that He gives it - and it is believed to be the last hour after Asr. (Sahih al-Bukhari 935). Many scholars also encourage reciting Surah al-Kahf on Friday.')
B.aOd=s(["eid","eid dua","eid mubarak","eid salah"],t.s)
B.bmE=new A.K(B.aOd,'The Prophet said: "Every nation has its festival, and this is ours" (Sahih al-Bukhari 952). He used to return from the Eid prayer by a different road from the one he went by (Sahih al-Bukhari 986). Allah says to complete the fast and glorify Him for His guidance (Qur\'an 2:185). The takbeer: "Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, la ilaha illallah, wallahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar wa lillahil hamd" - aloud on the roads, softly in the heart.')
B.aw0=s(["fasting shawwal","six days of shawwal","monday fasting","thursday fasting","white days","extra fasts","fast the year"],t.s)
B.bpK=new A.K(B.aw0,"Beyond Ramadan: fasting Ramadan then six days of Shawwal \"is like fasting the whole year\" (Sahih Muslim 1164). The Prophet fasted Mondays and Thursdays - deeds are presented on those days (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 747, hasan per Darussalam) - and the three white days, the 13th, 14th, and 15th of the lunar month (Abu Dawud 2449, sahih per al-Albani). The most beloved fast to Allah is Dawud's: a day on, a day off. (Sahih al-Bukhari 3420)")
B.F4=s(["suhoor","sehri","pre-dawn meal"],t.s)
B.bry=new A.K(B.F4,'"Take suhoor, for in suhoor there is blessing." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1923). Delay it toward dawn; the Prophet said the difference between our fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is the pre-dawn meal. (Muslim 1096). Even dates and water carry the barakah.')
B.axW=s(["itikaf","spiritual retreat","last ten nights"],t.s)
B.bot=new A.K(B.axW,"I'tikaf - secluding oneself in the masjid for worship - was practiced by the Prophet every Ramadan, ten days, and in the year he passed away, twenty (Sahih al-Bukhari 2044). Scholars differ on its minimum length, so ask a scholar of your madhhab; the essence is to leave the world at the door and keep only conversation with Allah.")
B.aNV=s(["feed a fasting person","feeding iftar","iftar for someone","feed"],t.s)
B.brH=new A.K(B.aNV,"\"Whoever provides the food for a fasting person to break his fast earns the same reward as his, without the fasting person's reward being diminished in any way.\" (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 807, sahih per Darussalam). A date and a glass of milk suffice - and the angels make du'a for the giver all that evening.")
B.arR=s(["rain dua","it's raining","rain blessing","rain shower","rain"],t.s)
B.bn5=new A.K(B.arR,"When the rain falls: \"Allahumma sayyiban nafi'an\" - O Allah, make it a beneficial rain. (Sahih al-Bukhari 1032). Rain is a good time to make du'a, as many scholars encourage.")
B.aKF=s(["wind dua","storm dua","strong wind","thunder dua","lightning","wind","storm"],t.s)
B.bnt=new A.K(B.aKF,"For the wind: \"Allahumma inni as'aluka khayraha, wa khayra ma fiiha, wa khayra ma ursilat bihi, wa a'udhu bika min sharriha...\" - O Allah, I ask You for its good, the good in it, the good it was sent with, and I seek refuge in You from its evil. (Sahih Muslim 899). The thunder glorifies the praise of its Lord - say Subhan Allah as it rolls (reported in Musnad Ahmad; number and grade not checked).")
B.aDS=s(["new moon","crescent moon","moon sighting","hilal","moon"],t.s)
B.bp6=new A.K(B.aDS,"Seeing the new crescent: \"Allahumma ahillahu 'alaina bil amni wal iman, was-salamati wal islam...\" - O Allah, let this moon rise over us with security, faith, safety, and Islam. (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3451, weak per Darussalam; at-Tirmidhi himself called it hasan gharib). The sighting ties the ummah to the sky - the month begins when the crescent is seen, not when the calendar guesses.")
B.avl=s(["halal income","halal earnings","haram money","riba","interest","halal work"],t.s)
B.bn8=new A.K(B.avl,'"O people, Allah is Pure and accepts only what is pure - He commands the believers as He commanded the messengers: eat of the good and do righteous work." (Sahih Muslim 1015). Earnings built on riba are fought by the Prophet himself: he cursed the one who consumes riba, the one who gives it, the one who records it, and its two witnesses - "they are alike." (Muslim 1598). Honest trade is a noble way to earn: the Prophet \ufdfa himself traded before he received revelation.')
B.aCU=s(["gambling","lottery","betting","casino","poker"],t.s)
B.bqv=new A.K(B.aCU,'"O you who have believed, indeed, intoxicants, gambling, ... and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid it that you may be successful. Satan only wants to cause between you animosity and hatred through intoxicants and gambling and to avert you from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer." (Al-Ma\'idah 90-91). The money of gambling is built on taking without consent - the blessed exit door is always open.')
B.arV=s(["alcohol","drinking","wine","beer","intoxicants"],t.s)
B.bqL=new A.K(B.arV,'"Every intoxicant is khamr, and every khamr is unlawful." (Sahih Muslim 2003). It is also reported that the prayer of one who drinks khamr is not accepted for forty days, and that Allah accepts his repentance if he repents (Jami at-Tirmidhi 1862 - graded da\'if by Darussalam; al-Tirmidhi himself called it hasan). What poisons the mind is barred from the body, whatever shape the bottle takes.')
B.aNg=s(["eating manners","right hand eating","wash hands eating","table manners islam","eat with the right hand","manners of eating","etiquette of eating"],t.s)
B.bpW=new A.K(B.aNg,"The Sunnah of the table: mention Allah's name, eat with the right hand, and eat from what is nearest to you (Sahih al-Bukhari 5376; see also Sahih Muslim 2017 and 2020). If you forget to mention Allah at the start, say: Bismillahi awwalahu wa akhirahu (Sunan Abi Dawud 3767, sahih per al-Albani). Washing the hands before and after the meal is reported to bring blessing in the food (Sunan Abi Dawud 3761 - graded da'if (weak) by al-Albani, so held as a weak report). Eat together and mention Allah's name: the Prophet \ufdfa told his Companions that the food would then be blessed for them (Sunan Abi Dawud 3764, hasan per al-Albani).")
B.aDT=s(["miswak","tooth stick","brush teeth sunnah"],t.s)
B.bom=new A.K(B.aDT,'"Were it not that I might overburden my ummah, I would have commanded them to use the miswak before every prayer." (Sahih al-Bukhari 887). The Prophet cleaned his teeth at wudu, before prayer, before reciting, on waking - a different part of worship than fresh breath alone.')
B.ash=s(["honey","black seed","tibben nabawi","prophetic medicine","natural remedy"],t.s)
B.bpv=new A.K(B.ash,'From the Sunnah of healing: honey - "healing for people" (An-Nahl 69), and the Prophet said healing is in three: the cut of the cupper, a drink of honey, and cauterization with fire - but he forbade his ummah cauterization. (Sahih al-Bukhari, Book of Medicine). And black seed: "the healing for every disease except death" (Bukhari 5688). Medicine of the body and the ruqyah of the heart travel together.')
B.aNl=s(["zamzam","drinking zamzam","umrah zamzam"],t.s)
B.bpn=new A.K(B.aNl,'"The water of Zamzam is for whatever it is drunk for" - drink it with an intention: knowledge, healing, forgiveness, a righteous child. (Sunan Ibn Majah 3062, hasan per Darussalam). It sprang for Ismail in the desert of Makkah and has not ceased - five thousand years of answered thirst.')
B.aKr=s(["cupping","hijamah","blood cupping"],t.s)
B.bmy=new A.K(B.aKr,"Cupping (hijamah) is a traditional treatment that many scholars count as part of prophetic medicine. Even treatment has an etiquette: seek the skilled, pay fairly, and pair it with du'a. Ask a trained practitioner, and your doctor if you have a medical condition.")
B.av3=s(["cats","kittens","pet cat"],t.s)
B.bqs=new A.K(B.av3,"Kindness to cats is from the Sunnah: cats are not impure, the Prophet said; they are among those who go about among you, and water a cat has drunk from remains usable. (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 92, sahih per Darussalam).")
B.aAU=s(["going to sleep","bedtime","sleep on right side","wake up dua","waking up","sleep"],t.s)
B.boA=new A.K(B.aAU,'Before sleep: wudu as you washed for prayer, lie on the right side, and recite Ayat al-Kursi - "a protector from Allah is appointed over you, and no devil comes near you until morning." (Sahih al-Bukhari 2311). Dust the bedding three times - "for you do not know what came to rest upon it." (Bukhari 6320). Waking: "Alhamdulillahilladhi ahyana ba\'da ma amatana wa ilaihin nushur" - all praise to Allah who gave us life after death, and to Him is the resurrection. (Bukhari 6312)')
B.aEV=s(["seeing someone sick","someone else afflicted","heard bad news"],t.s)
B.bq4=new A.K(B.aEV,"When you see someone afflicted: \"Alhamdulillahil-ladhi 'afani mimabtalaaka bihi wa faddalani 'ala kathirin mimman khalaqa tafdila\" - praise to Allah who spared me what He afflicted you with and favored me over much of His creation. (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3431, weak per Darussalam). Gratitude without the afflicted hearing it; the reward and the mercy both remain.")
B.aCI=s(["mourning period","how long is the mourning period","how long to mourn","how long should i mourn","widow waiting period","iddah of a widow","widows iddah","how long is mourning"],t.s)
B.bnr=new A.K(B.aCI,"Allah says of wives whose husbands die: \u201cthey, [the wives, shall] wait four months and ten [days].\u201d (Qur'an 2:234). The Prophet \ufdfa taught that outward mourning for any dead person is three days, and for a husband it is four months and ten days (Sahih al-Bukhari 1280). Grief itself has no timetable and is not a sin. For how the waiting period is kept in your own situation, please ask a qualified scholar.")
B.aLe=s(["someone died","death of a loved one","lost my mother","lost my father","grief","mourning","funeral","visiting graves","passed away","died","lost my mum","lost my mom","lost my parent","lost my parents","lost my son","lost my daughter","lost my husband","lost my wife","lost my brother","lost my sister","lost my grandmother","lost my grandfather","lost a loved one"],t.s)
B.brK=new A.K(B.aLe,'When death takes someone you love: "Inna lillahi wa inna ilaihi raji\'un - Allahumma\'jurni fi musibati wakhluf li khayran minha" - To Allah we belong and to Him we return; O Allah, reward me in my calamity and replace it for me with better. (Sahih Muslim 918). The Prophet said: "Allah says to the angels: build for My servant a palace in Paradise and call it the House of Praise." For the deceased: wash, shroud, pray over, and bury - attending carries the reward of two great qirats. (Bukhari 1325) And visit the graves - "they remind you of the Hereafter" (Muslim 977). Say to the grieving: "May Allah magnify your reward, beautify your patience, and forgive your departed."')
B.aww=s(["trust in allah","tawakkul","my rizq","provision","how will i survive","jobless","no money","money"],t.s)
B.br4=new A.K(B.aww,'The Prophet said: "If you relied upon Allah as He should be relied upon, He would provide for you as He provides for the birds - they leave in the morning with empty stomachs and return full." (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 2344, hasan per Darussalam). And: "Tie your camel, then trust in Allah." (Tirmidhi 2517, hasan per Darussalam). Tawakkul is not the abandonment of means - it is the heart\'s grip on Allah while the hand grips the rope. Rizq is written for each person when the angel is sent to breathe in the soul, after three stages of forty days in the womb (Sahih al-Bukhari 3208, Sahih Muslim 2643); what is yours will walk to you.')
B.awn=s(["hurt myself","want to die","end my life","no point living","self harm","suicidal","don't want to live","kill myself","no will to live"],t.s)
B.bni=new A.K(B.awn,'Please - stop, and breathe. Your pain is real, and so is Allah\'s promise: "Allah does not charge a soul except [with that within] its capacity" (Al-Baqarah 286), and "do not despair of the mercy of Allah" (Az-Zumar 53). This world can hurt unbearably, but the Prophet said: "No fatigue, nor illness, nor anxiety, nor sorrow, nor harm reaches a Muslim but that Allah expiates by it - even a thorn." (Sahih al-Bukhari 5641). You are not alone. If you might act on these thoughts, please call your local emergency number or a crisis line right now, or go to someone near you; the Sakina room lists help lines. Stay - the One who made you is not done with you.')
B.aAg=s(["hijab","covering","modesty dress","why do muslim women cover"],t.s)
B.bpS=new A.K(B.aAg,'Allah says: "And tell the believing women to reduce [some] of their vision and guard their private parts and not expose their adornment except that which [necessarily] appears thereof and to wrap [a portion of] their headcovers over their chests..." (An-Nur 31), and: "O Prophet, tell your wives and your daughters and the women of the believers to bring down over themselves [part] of their outer garments." (Al-Ahzab 59). The Prophet \ufdfa is reported to have told Asma\' that once a woman reaches puberty, nothing should be shown of her but this and this - and he pointed to his face and hands (Sunan Abi Dawud 4104 - Abu Dawud himself called it mursal, meaning a link in the chain is missing; al-Albani graded it sahih; scholars differ on how it applies, so ask a scholar of your madhhab). It is worship, obedience, and - for many who wear it - peace.')
B.aEY=s(["memorize quran","hifz","memorization tips","learn quran","quran study tips","memorize"],t.s)
B.bow=new A.K(B.aEY,'The memorizer\'s method, unchanged for a thousand years: a daily portion - new and revision - with recitation to a teacher who corrects. Ibn al-Jazari said: "Committing to what you can bear - even a little - is better than burning out on a lot." Recite in the same copy, at the same hour, and listen to one reciter only until the passage settles. The promise is sealed in the hadith: "The best of you are those who learn the Qur\'an and teach it." (Sahih al-Bukhari 5027)')
B.aLW=s(["tajweed","pronunciation quran","recitation rules","makhraj"],t.s)
B.bmR=new A.K(B.aLW,"Tajweed is giving every letter its right: from its makhraj - its exit point - and with its sifah - its characteristics - slowly, without artificiality. Begin with one surah perfected; the Qur'an itself teaches: \"And recite the Qur'an with measured recitation.\" (Al-Muzzammil 4)")
B.apQ=s(["learn arabic","arabic alphabet","arabic learning tips","arabic"],t.s)
B.bnL=new A.K(B.apQ,"The alphabet is a door, not a mountain: twenty-nine letters, each with a shape at the start, middle, and end of a word. The Wasia Academy in this app walks children through every letter with sound and practice - and what works for them works for you: one letter a day, said aloud, written twice, found in a word you already know. Ten weeks of one letter a day, and the script that carried the revelation is yours.")
B.aJf=s(["adam","first human","adam and eve","hawa"],t.s)
B.bpu=new A.K(B.aJf,"Adam - the first human and the first prophet - was taught the names of all things by Allah Himself (Al-Baqarah 31). From Adam and Hawwa came every nation; from their repentance we learn that the door of return never closes, for them or for us.")
B.aGR=s(["nuh","noah","the flood","ark"],t.s)
B.bq0=new A.K(B.aGR,"Nuh, peace be upon him, called his people by day in openness and by night in secret - for nine hundred and fifty years (Al-Ankabut 14). When the flood came, the ark carried the believers and pairs of every kind. The lesson: success is measured by faithfulness to the message, not by who listens.")
B.aqg=s(["ibrahim","abraham","kaaba builder","friend of allah"],t.s)
B.brp=new A.K(B.aqg,'Ibrahim, Khalilullah - the Friend of Allah - smashed the idols his people worshipped and walked out of the fire they lit for him - Ibn Abbas reported that he said "Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer" (Sahih al-Bukhari 4563), words the Qur\'an also gives to the believers: "Sufficient for us is Allah, and [He is] the best Disposer of affairs." (Al-Imran 173). He and his son Ismail raised the foundations of the Ka\'bah together (Al-Baqarah 127). Every prophet after him is of his house, and we send peace upon him in every prayer.')
B.aKW=s(["yusuf","joseph","best of stories"],t.s)
B.bqZ=new A.K(B.aKW,"Yusuf was thrown into a well by his own brothers, sold as a slave, slandered by a minister's wife, and imprisoned - then raised to the treasury of Egypt. The Qur'an calls his story the best of stories (Yusuf 3). Its thread: no betrayal outruns Allah's plan, and forgiveness is the crown of the wronged - \"No blame will there be upon you today.\" (Yusuf 92).")
B.aGw=s(["musa","moses","red sea","pharaoh","firawn"],t.s)
B.brL=new A.K(B.aGw,"Musa, the one Allah spoke to directly (An-Nisa 164), stood before Pharaoh with a staff and a brother - and the sea split at his strike (Ash-Shuara 63). He received the Tawrah on the mountain and led Bani Israel through forty years of lessons. When Khidr outpaced his patience, Musa learned: knowledge is deeper than what we see (Al-Kahf 60-82).")
B.aFC=s(["dawud","david","zabur","psalms"],t.s)
B.bql=new A.K(B.aFC,'Dawud was given the Zabur - the Psalms - and iron was softened for him: "Make full coats of mail and calculate [precisely] the links" (Saba 10-11). Mountains and birds would echo his glorification with him (Saba 10). He judged between people with justice and repented at speed when rebuked by two disputants.')
B.asZ=s(["sulayman","solomon","kingdom","jinn and animals"],t.s)
B.bnZ=new A.K(B.asZ,"Sulayman inherited Dawud's kingdom and was given what no one after him was given: the wind traveled a month's journey each morning and evening for him, the jinn built at his command, and even the ants had a language he understood (An-Naml 16-19). He asked for a kingdom no one after him would have - and it was given (Sad 35).")
B.aIb=s(["isa","jesus","mary","messiah"],t.s)
B.bnh=new A.K(B.aIb,'Isa, the Messiah, was born to the virgin Maryam - she was dedicated to the temple by her mother and miraculously sustained (Al-Imran 35-37; Maryam 16-34). He spoke in the cradle, healed by Allah\'s leave, and called to worship Allah alone: "Indeed, Allah is my Lord and your Lord, so worship Him" (Maryam 36). The Qur\'an says plainly: he is the messenger of Allah, His word to Maryam, not a son - "Exalted is He above having a son" (An-Nisa 171).')
B.aNz=s(["muhammad","life of the prophet","the prophet's story","seerah summary","final prophet"],t.s)
B.bp0=new A.K(B.aNz,'Muhammad ibn Abdullah, the Seal of the Prophets (Al-Ahzab 40), was born in Makkah in the Year of the Elephant, orphaned young, known as As-Sadiq Al-Amin - the Truthful, the Trustworthy - long before revelation. At forty, in the cave of Hira, Jibreel brought him: "Iqra" - Read. He endured thirteen years of Makkan persecution, walked to Madinah when the assassination plot was laid, and in ten years there built a community that changed history - forgiving the city that stoned him at its conquest: "Go, you are free." He passed at sixty-three with his armor pledged for wheat - leaving no gold and a religion that now carries two billion hearts.')
B.au_=s(["order of prophets","list of prophets","25 prophets","how many prophets","prophets mentioned"],t.s)
B.bnD=new A.K(B.au_,"The Qur'an names twenty-five prophets; from Adam, the first, to Muhammad, the last. The named ones: Adam, Idris, Nuh, Hud, Salih, Ibrahim, Lut, Ismail, Ishaq, Ya'qub, Yusuf, Ayyub, Shu'ayb, Musa, Harun, Dhul-Kifl, Dawud, Sulayman, Ilyas, Al-Yasa, Yunus, Zakariya, Yahya, Isa, and Muhammad - peace be upon them all. The stories shelf of this app walks many of them, story by story.")
B.aDW=s(["difference between prophet and messenger","nabi vs rasul","messenger vs prophet"],t.s)
B.bqG=new A.K(B.aDW,"A prophet (nabi) receives revelation from Allah. A messenger (rasul) is a prophet sent with a book or a law to a people - every messenger is a prophet, but not every prophet was entrusted with a new scripture. The five of strongest resolve (ulu al-'azm) are Nuh, Ibrahim, Musa, Isa, and Muhammad - peace be upon them all.")
B.atZ=s(["fatiha","opening chapter","first surah"],t.s)
B.boe=new A.K(B.atZ,"Al-Fatiha - the Opening - is the seven verses no prayer stands without: the Prophet \ufdfa said the one who does not recite the Opening of the Book has not validly performed the prayer (Sahih Muslim 394). It is Umm al-Qur'an, and he said the like of it was not revealed in the Tawrah, the Injil, the Zabur or the Furqan (Jami at-Tirmidhi 2875, sahih per Darussalam).")
B.auR=s(["ayat al-kursi","kursi","greatest verse","throne verse"],t.s)
B.bn_=new A.K(B.auR,'Ayat al-Kursi (Al-Baqarah 255) is regarded as the greatest verse of the Qur\'an, and it is widely recited after every obligatory prayer and before sleep. Its beginning: "Allah - there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of all."')
B.arP=s(["ya-sin","yaseen","heart of the quran"],t.s)
B.bqj=new A.K(B.arP,"Ya-Sin is the heart of the Qur'an, as the Prophet named it (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 2887, weak per Darussalam). Because that report is weak, practices attached to it (reciting it for the dying or over a need) are not presented here as Sunnah: ask a scholar.")
B.aBg=s(["al-mulk","surah mulk"],t.s)
B.bpw=new A.K(B.aBg,"Surah Al-Mulk (The Sovereignty) is reported to be a surah of thirty verses that pleads for its reciter until he is forgiven (Sunan Abi Dawud 1400, hasan per al-Albani; Jami at-Tirmidhi 2891, hasan per Darussalam). A separate report says it delivers from the punishment of the grave (Jami at-Tirmidhi 2890 - graded da'if by Darussalam; al-Tirmidhi himself called it hasan gharib).")
B.aLp=s(["al-ikhlas","ikhlas","qul huwallahu"],t.s)
B.bqH=new A.K(B.aLp,"Qul Huwallahu Ahad - Al-Ikhlas, the Sincerity - is said to equal a third of the Qur'an (Sahih al-Bukhari 5013). Four verses that name Allah: The One, the Eternal Refuge, who begets not and was not begotten - and nothing is comparable to Him.")
B.aGM=s(["last two verses of baqarah","kursi dua night","suffice him"],t.s)
B.bpq=new A.K(B.aGM,"Whoever recites the last two verses of Al-Baqarah at night, they will suffice him (Sahih al-Bukhari 5009). At bedtime the Prophet \ufdfa also cupped his hands, recited the three Quls into them, blew into them and wiped what he could of his body, three times (Sahih al-Bukhari 5017).")
B.aDR=s(["recitation reward","letter of quran reward","reading quran reward"],t.s)
B.bp1=new A.K(B.aDR,'The reciter is not paid by the page but by the letter: "Whoever recites a letter of the Book of Allah has a reward for it, and each reward is multiplied ten times - I do not say alif-lam-mim is a letter, but alif is a letter..." (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 2910, hasan per Darussalam). A slow page outearns a rushed volume.')
B.azA=s(["compiled quran","who compiled the quran","uthman","quran history"],t.s)
B.bnc=new A.K(B.azA,"Revelation ended with the Prophet's passing, and the compilation followed: Abu Bakr gathered the Qur'an into one book after the Battle of Yamamah, at Umar's insistence (Sahih al-Bukhari 4986). Uthman standardized the consonantal text and sent copies to the cities - the manuscripts we read descend from those. Allah promised the preservation Himself: \"Indeed, it is We who sent down the Qur'an and indeed, We will be its guardian\" (Al-Hijr 9).")
B.aMn=s(["al-waqiah","waqiah","rizq surah","poverty surah"],t.s)
B.bn4=new A.K(B.aMn,"The tradition says recite Surah Al-Waqi'ah - the Event, the surah of provision - between Maghrib and Isha for sufficiency from poverty (reported by Ibn Masud in the collections of ad-Darimi and others). Its opening strikes the heart: when the inevitable event arrives...")
B.aHR=s(["names of allah meanings","names of allah","asma ul husna","attributes of allah","who is allah","meanings of the names"],t.s)
B.bre=new A.K(B.aHR,"The Prophet said Allah has ninety-nine names - one hundred less one - whoever preserves them enters Paradise (Sahih al-Bukhari 2736). A few of their lights: Ar-Rahman - the Entirely Merciful; Ar-Rahim - the Especially Merciful to believers; Al-Malik - the King; Al-Quddus - the Most Holy; Al-Wadud - the Most Loving; Al-Latif - the Most Subtle and Kind; Al-Khabir - the All-Aware; Al-Fattah - the Opener; Al-Alim - the All-Knowing; Al-Hakim - the All-Wise; Al-Ghafoor - the Ever-Forgiving; As-Sabur - the Most Patient; Al-Wakeel - the Best Disposer of Affairs; Al-Hayy - the Ever-Living; Al-Qayyum - the Sustainer; An-Nur - the Light; Al-Haqq - the Absolute Truth; Al-Mateen - the Firm. The 99 Names game walks them one by one with meanings and references.")
B.aH5=s(["ghusl","full bath","janabah","major impurity","after intimacy"],t.s)
B.bpz=new A.K(B.aH5,"Ghusl - the full wash - is owed after intimacy, after menstruation, and after post-natal bleeding. The Prophet's way: wash the hands, rinse the mouth and nose, wash the head and right side then left - as one continuous wash. (Sahih al-Bukhari 248). Water reaches every part, once or more.")
B.aDP=s(["tayammum","no water","dust ablution","dry wudu"],t.s)
B.brg=new A.K(B.aDP,'When water is absent - or using it would harm you - Allah permitted tayammum: "then seek clean earth and wipe over your faces and your hands [with it]" (An-Nisa 43). Strike clean dust with the palms, wipe the face, then the hands to the elbows (Al-Ma\'idah 6). The earth itself is made for purification, said the Prophet. (Sahih al-Bukhari 344)')
B.ax7=s(["breaks wudu","nullify wudu","invalid wudu","wudu broken"],t.s)
B.bmS=new A.K(B.ax7,"What nullifies wudu: anything that exits the two private passes; deep sleep; and loss of consciousness or sanity. Scholars differ on touching the private part: one report says to make wudu after it (Sunan Abi Dawud 181, sahih per al-Albani) and another likens it to any other part of the body (Jami at-Tirmidhi 85, sahih per Darussalam); ask a scholar of your madhhab. Doubt does not remove certainty of purity (Sahih Muslim 362). Scholars also differ on eating camel meat, so ask a scholar.")
B.aoj=s(["period","menstruation","hayd","can I pray on my period","menses"],t.s)
B.bnv=new A.K(B.aoj,"The menstruating woman does not pray and does not fast - the Prophet told Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh: leave prayer during the days, then wash and pray. (Sahih al-Bukhari 306) She makes up the fasts, not the prayers: the Prophet \ufdfa did not order women to make up the prayers they missed in their periods (Sahih al-Bukhari 321). Worship does not stop - dhikr, du'a, Qur'an listening and good deeds all remain open.")
B.aF6=s(["missed prayer","make up prayer","qada prayer","overslept prayer","forgot prayer"],t.s)
B.brn=new A.K(B.aF6,'Whoever sleeps through a prayer or forgets it, let him pray it when he remembers - "there is no expiation for it except this" (Sahih al-Bukhari 597). That is for a prayer missed through sleep or forgetting. A woman does not make up the prayers she misses in her period or in postpartum bleeding: the Prophet \ufdfa did not order women to make up those prayers (Sahih al-Bukhari 321). For a long backlog of missed prayers, or the order to pray them in, scholars give details that I do not have verified text for, so please ask a scholar about your own case.')
B.ay5=s(["combine prayers","travel prayers","jam","qasr","shorten prayer travel"],t.s)
B.bs_=new A.K(B.ay5,'The traveler shortens the four-unit prayers to two - a gift of the Sunnah the Prophet said is charity Allah gave: "It is a charity Allah has given you, so accept His charity." (Sahih Muslim 686) And on a real journey he combined - Zuhr with Asr, Maghrib with Isha - as he did at Arafat and Muzdalifah (Sahih Muslim 1218).')
B.aIW=s(["congregation","jamaah","pray together","mosque prayer","pray in the masjid"],t.s)
B.boC=new A.K(B.aIW,"Prayer in congregation outweighs solitary prayer by twenty-seven degrees (Sahih al-Bukhari 645). The mu'adhdhin calls, the rows form shoulder to shoulder, the imam leads - and the angels pray behind the rows. Twenty-seven: the scholars said it is as if a man prayed every day and night for five and twenty.")
B.aMt=s(["adhan","call to prayer","muadhin","repeat after adhan"],t.s)
B.bqV=new A.K(B.aMt,'When the adhan sounds, repeat the words after the mu\'adhdhin - then send blessings upon the Prophet, and ask for al-Wasilah: "O Allah, Lord of this perfect call and the established prayer, grant Muhammad the Wasilah..." (Sahih Muslim 384). "My intercession will be obligatory for him" - it was said of whoever asks it once. (Bukhari 614)')
B.ato=s(["khuffs","leather socks","wipe socks","masah","winter socks"],t.s)
B.bnm=new A.K(B.ato,"The traveler wipes over leather socks for three days and nights, the resident for one day and night - then the wash is owed. (Sahih Muslim 276) Ali said he saw the Prophet \ufdfa wipe the top of his leather socks, and that if religion were by opinion the underside would seem more fitting to wipe (Sunan Abi Dawud 162, sahih per al-Albani).")
B.azC=s(["tawhid","oneness of allah","three types of tawhid","uluhiyyah"],t.s)
B.bmq=new A.K(B.azC,'Tawhid is that Allah alone is God - in His lordship (Ar-Rububiyyah: He alone creates and sustains), in His worship (Al-Uluhiyyah: Him alone we worship and invoke), and in His names and attributes (Al-Asma was-Sifat: as He described Himself, without likeness). "Allah witnesses that there is no deity except Him, and [so do] the angels and those of knowledge" (Al-Imran 18).')
B.aKN=s(["shirk","polytheism","associating partners"],t.s)
B.bqh=new A.K(B.aKN,'Shirk - joining partners with Allah - is the gravest of sins: "Indeed, Allah does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills" (An-Nisa 48). It is not only idols - scholars warn that showing off in worship (riya\') is a hidden form of shirk. The cure is what the caller to Islam repeats: La ilaha illallah.')
B.aNA=s(["qadar","destiny","predestination","qadr","why did allah allow"],t.s)
B.bpt=new A.K(B.aNA,'Belief in qadar - the decree - is the sixth pillar of faith. The Prophet told the slave seeking freedom: "Say: I trust in Allah, there is no might nor power except with Allah" - and taught that this saying is a rescue from every hardship. (Sahih al-Bukhari) And he said you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another (Sahih Muslim 54). What reached you could never have missed you; what missed you could never have reached you.')
B.aBO=s(["angels","jibreel","gabriel","recording angels","mika'il"],t.s)
B.bof=new A.K(B.aBO,'Belief in the angels is the second pillar of faith. Jibreel brings revelation; Mika\'il is charged with rain and provision; Israfil will blow the Trumpet; Malik keeps the Fire; and Kiraman Katibin - the noble scribes - record every word: "Man does not utter any word except that with him is an observer prepared [to record]" (Qaf 18). (See Al-Baqarah 97-98, Fatir 1, Az-Zukhruf 77)')
B.aDG=s(["jinn","qarin","evil spirits","demons"],t.s)
B.bqW=new A.K(B.aDG,'The jinn were created before man from fire: "from scorching fire" (Al-Hijr 27), "from a smokeless flame of fire" (Ar-Rahman 15) - some believers, some not. The Prophet \ufdfa said that every one of us has a companion from the jinn assigned to him; asked whether that included him, he said yes, but Allah helped him against it so it only urges him to good (Sahih Muslim 2814). Their harm is real but bounded. Reciting Ayat al-Kursi before sleep brings a protector from Allah and no devil comes near until morning (Sahih al-Bukhari 2311), and the last two verses of Al-Baqarah at night will suffice him (Sahih al-Bukhari 5009).')
B.aOI=s(["magic","sihr","spell","witchcraft","someone did magic on me"],t.s)
B.bpj=new A.K(B.aOI,"Sihr is real - the two angels Harut and Marut taught the test, and people learn from them that \"by which they cause separation between a man and his wife\" (Al-Baqarah 102). The Prophet was affected by a spell and was healed by Jibreel with the Mu'awwidhat. (Sahih al-Bukhari 5763) The defense is not fear but remembrance: the three Quls, Ayat al-Kursi, and the dua \"Bismillahilladhi la yadurru ma'a ismihi shay'un...\" (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3388, hasan per Darussalam) - nothing harms the one who says them morning and evening.")
B.aD_=s(["bid'ah","innovation","newly invented","bida"],t.s)
B.brv=new A.K(B.aD_,"\"The worst of matters are the newly invented; every innovation is misguidance, and every misguidance is in the Fire.\" (Sahih Muslim 867). This is why the companions guarded the practice so carefully - what was not worship in the Prophet's day is not worship in ours. And yet the doors of mercy remain wide: whatever eases people without contradicting the revelation finds its place in the scholars' categories.")
B.aNG=s(["non-muslim family","non muslim parents","my non muslim","christian family","jewish friends"],t.s)
B.bpU=new A.K(B.aNG,'Allah said: "Allah does not forbid you from those who do not fight you because of religion and do not expel you from your homes - from being righteous toward them and acting justly toward them. Indeed, Allah loves those who act justly" (Al-Mumtahanah 8). Kindness to parents is owed even if they do not share your faith: " accompany them in this world with appropriate kindness" (Luqman 15) - while worship remains Allah\'s alone.')
B.aFK=s(["fidya","cannot fast","unable to fast","old age fasting","pregnant fasting"],t.s)
B.bn6=new A.K(B.aFK,'For the one who cannot fast from old age or lasting illness: "a ransom [as substitute] of feeding a poor person [each day]" (Al-Baqarah 184); Ibn Abbas said this verse was not abrogated for the old man and old woman who cannot fast (Sahih al-Bukhari 4505). The pregnant or nursing woman who fears for herself or her child: scholars differ on whether she makes the fast up, feeds a poor person, or both - ask a scholar. Fiqh is mercy before it is arithmetic.')
B.aBZ=s(["wasiyyah","write a will","write my will","my will","estate","one third will"],t.s)
B.bo5=new A.K(B.aBZ,'The Prophet heard that Sa\'d wished to bequeath all his wealth: "One third, and one third is much - to leave your heirs rich is better than leaving them poor, begging from people." (Sahih al-Bukhari 2742) A wasiyyah is made for non-heirs - up to a third - and debt is settled before any inheritance moves.')
B.aO9=s(["faraid","inheritance","who inherits","islamic inheritance"],t.s)
B.bnH=new A.K(B.aO9,"It is reported that the Prophet \ufdfa told Abu Hurairah to learn the rules of inheritance and teach them, for they are half of knowledge (Sunan Ibn Majah 2719 - graded da'if (weak) by Darussalam, so held as a weak report). The shares are fixed in An-Nisa 11-12: the son's share, the daughter's half, the spouse's quarter or eighth, the parents' sixths - apportioned after the burial, the debt, and the wasiyyah. It was a science the companions called half of knowledge because families stand or split on it.")
B.aFt=s(["wudu","ablution","how to make wudu","wudhu","wuzu","wudoo"],t.s)
B.bsi=new A.K(B.aFt,"Wudu has six obligatory steps: (1) intention, (2) washing the face, (3) washing the hands to the elbows, (4) wiping the head, (5) washing the feet to the ankles, (6) maintaining sequence. The Prophet \ufdfa said that whoever performs wudu well, his sins come out of his body, even from beneath his fingernails (Sahih Muslim 245).")
B.au2=s(["wudu nullifiers","breaks wudu","break my wudu","nullify wudu","invalidate wudu","invalidates wudu","lost wudu"],t.s)
B.boW=new A.K(B.au2,"Wudu is nullified by: (1) anything exiting the private parts, (2) deep sleep, (3) loss of consciousness, (4) according to many scholars, touching the private parts directly with the hand (the Hanafi school disagrees). Differences like this are why it is best to learn wudu from a teacher of your own school.")
B.aqU=s(["tayammum","dry ablution","no water","sand prayer"],t.s)
B.bnN=new A.K(B.aqU,'If water is unavailable or harmful to use, perform tayammum: strike clean earth once with both hands, wipe the face, then wipe the back of the hands. Allah says: "And if you are ill or on a journey or one of you comes from the place of relieving himself or you have contacted women and find no water, then seek clean earth." (Qur\'an 4:43, 5:6).')
B.aIi=s(["ghusl","ritual bath","janabah","major impurity"],t.s)
B.brS=new A.K(B.aIi,'Ghusl requires: (1) intention, (2) washing the entire body including the mouth and nose. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "When a person performs ghusl, let him rinse his mouth and nose." (Sahih al-Bukhari 248). It is obligatory after sexual relations, menstruation, postpartum bleeding, and ejaculation.')
B.aIg=s(["fajr","dawn prayer","morning prayer","subh"],t.s)
B.bpm=new A.K(B.aIg,'Fajr is two rak\'ahs, prayed from true dawn until sunrise. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Whoever prays the two cool prayers (Fajr and Asr) will enter Paradise." (Sahih al-Bukhari 574). It is the prayer most often missed, so many people set a second alarm and sleep early.')
B.aJt=s(["dhuhr","zuhr","noon prayer","midday prayer"],t.s)
B.br5=new A.K(B.aJt,"Dhuhr is four rak'ahs, prayed after the sun passes its zenith until the shadow of an object equals its length (plus the zenith shadow). The Prophet \ufdfa said that prayer is light (Sahih Muslim 223).")
B.at2=s(["asr","afternoon prayer"],t.s)
B.bs9=new A.K(B.at2,"Asr is four rak'ahs, prayed from when the shadow of an object equals its length until sunset. Some scholars encourage voluntary rak'ahs before it. Missing Asr on purpose is a grave loss, so guard it.")
B.aqn=s(["maghrib","sunset prayer","evening prayer"],t.s)
B.bpJ=new A.K(B.aqn,'Maghrib is three rak\'ahs, prayed immediately after sunset until twilight disappears. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "My Ummah will continue to be upon good as long as they hasten to break the fast and delay the suhur." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1957). Hastening Maghrib is from the sunnah.')
B.aOw=s(["isha","night prayer"],t.s)
B.brq=new A.K(B.aOw,'Isha is four rak\'ahs, prayed from the disappearance of twilight until midnight (or until dawn). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "If someone prays Isha in congregation, it is as if he prayed half the night. And if he prays Fajr in congregation, it is as if he prayed the entire night." (Sahih Muslim 656).')
B.avh=s(["sujood sahw","forgetfulness prostration","mistake in prayer"],t.s)
B.bng=new A.K(B.avh,"If you add, omit, or doubt a part of prayer, perform two prostrations of forgetfulness (sujood as-sahw) before the taslim. The Prophet \ufdfa prayed Zuhr with five rak'ahs, then performed two prostrations after the taslim when reminded. (Sahih al-Bukhari 401, Sahih Muslim 572).")
B.aNS=s(["qada","make up prayers","missed prayer","qaza"],t.s)
B.bs8=new A.K(B.aNS,'A prayer missed through sleep or forgetting is prayed when it is remembered. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "When any of you sleeps through the prayer or forgets it, let him pray it when he remembers." (Sahih al-Bukhari 597, Sahih Muslim 684). There is no expiation except performing the prayer itself. A woman does not make up the prayers of her period or postpartum bleeding: the Prophet \ufdfa did not order women to make up those prayers (Sahih al-Bukhari 321). For a long backlog or the order of several prayers, please ask a scholar about your own case.')
B.aLk=s(["taraweeh","tarawih","night ramadan prayer"],t.s)
B.brl=new A.K(B.aLk,"Taraweeh is the night prayer of Ramadan, prayed in sets of two rak'ahs. The Prophet \ufdfa prayed it in the mosque for a few nights with people joining him, then stayed away fearing it would become obligatory for them (Sahih al-Bukhari 1129, Sahih Muslim 761). Umar later gathered the people behind one reciter, Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and called it a good innovation (Sahih al-Bukhari 2010).")
B.aKf=s(["witr","witr prayer","odd prayer"],t.s)
B.bqk=new A.K(B.aKf,"Witr is one rak'ah prayed after Isha, typically after Tahajjud or Taraweeh. It is a strongly emphasised sunnah in most schools and wajib in the Hanafi school.")
B.aqz=s(["tahajjud","night prayer","qiyam al-layl","tahajud"],t.s)
B.bpo=new A.K(B.aqz,'Tahajjud is the voluntary night prayer, best performed in the last third of the night. Allah says: "Indeed, the righteous will be among gardens and springs, accepting what their Lord has given them. Indeed, they were before that doers of good. They used to sleep but little of the night, and in the hours before dawn they would ask forgiveness." (Qur\'an 51:15-18).')
B.aJ2=s(["janazah","funeral prayer","dead prayer"],t.s)
B.brX=new A.K(B.aJ2,'The funeral prayer (Salat al-Janazah) is a communal obligation (fard kifayah). It has four takbirs: (1) after the first, recite Fatiha; (2) after the second, send blessings on the Prophet; (3) after the third, make dua for the deceased; (4) after the fourth, say salam. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Whoever follows a funeral until the prayer is offered will have one qirat of reward." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1325).')
B.aNv=s(["eid prayer","eid salat","salat al eid"],t.s)
B.bsj=new A.K(B.aNv,"Eid prayer is two rak'ahs with extra takbirs: seven in the first rak'ah and five in the second (before recitation). The Prophet \ufdfa said: \"Every nation has its day of celebration, and this is our day of celebration.\" (Sahih al-Bukhari 952, Sahih Muslim 892). It is recommended for women, children, and menstruating women to attend.")
B.aJB=s(["dua before sleep","sleeping dua","night dua","bedtime dua","dua for sleep","dua before bed","dua for bedtime","dua at bedtime","what to say before sleeping","what to say before bed","dua for going to sleep"],t.s)
B.bri=new A.K(B.aJB,'Before sleeping, say: "Bismika Allahumma amutu wa ahya" (In Your name, O Allah, I die and I live) (Sahih Muslim 2711). Make wudu and lie on your right side (Sahih al-Bukhari 247, Sahih Muslim 2710). The Prophet \ufdfa also placed his right hand under his cheek and said: "Allahumma qini adhabaka yawma tab\'athu ibadaka" (O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants) (Sunan Abi Dawud 5045, sahih per al-Albani). The Daily Duas in the Wasia Academy have Before Sleep pages, and For Your Heart has a Tired page with a du\'a for the night.\n[GO:/academy/hisn]\n[GO:/feelings]')
B.axP=s(["dua after waking","morning dua","waking up"],t.s)
B.boy=new A.K(B.axP,'Upon waking, say: "Alhamdu lillahi alladhi ahyana ba\'da ma amatana wa ilayhi an-nushur" (All praise is for Allah who gave us life after having taken it from us, and to Him is the resurrection). (Sahih al-Bukhari 6324, Sahih Muslim 2711).')
B.aLI=s(["dua before eating","eating dua","food dua"],t.s)
B.boB=new A.K(B.aLI,'Before eating, say: "Bismillah." If you forget, say: "Bismillahi fi awwalihi wa akhirihi" (In the name of Allah at its beginning and at its end). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "When one of you eats, let him mention the name of Allah. If he forgets at the beginning, let him say: Bismillahi fi awwalihi wa akhirihi." (Sunan al-Tirmidhi 1858, sahih per Darussalam).')
B.arE=s(["dua after eating","finished eating"],t.s)
B.bqY=new A.K(B.arE,"After eating, say: \"Alhamdu lillahi alladhi at'amani hadha wa razaqanihi min ghayri hawlin minni wa la quwwah\" (All praise is for Allah who fed me this and provided it for me without any might or power from me). (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3458, hasan per Darussalam).")
B.ayJ=s(["dua entering home","entering house","coming home"],t.s)
B.boS=new A.K(B.ayJ,'When entering your home, say: "Bismillahi walajna, wa bismillahi kharajna, wa \'ala rabbina tawakkalna" (In the name of Allah we enter, and in the name of Allah we leave, and upon our Lord we rely). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Then say: Allahumma inni as\'aluka khayra al-mawliji wa khayra al-makhraji" (O Allah, I ask You for the best of entering and the best of leaving). (Sunan Abi Dawud 5096, weak per al-Albani).')
B.aBF=s(["dua leaving home","leaving house","going out"],t.s)
B.bs4=new A.K(B.aBF,'When leaving home, say: "Bismillahi, tawakkaltu \'ala Allah, la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah" (In the name of Allah, I place my trust in Allah; there is no might and no power except with Allah). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "It will be said to him: You are guided, sufficed, and protected." (Sunan Abi Dawud 5095, sahih per al-Albani).')
B.aA7=s(["dua for travel","traveling dua","safar"],t.s)
B.bqi=new A.K(B.aA7,'When traveling, say: "Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar. Subhana alladhi sakhkhara lana hadha wa ma kunna lahu muqrinin, wa inna ila rabbina lamunqalibun" (Allah is the Greatest x3. Glory be to Him who has subjected this to us, and we could not have done it. And indeed we will return to our Lord). (Sahih Muslim 1342).')
B.atz=s(["dua for rizq","provision dua","money dua","wealth dua"],t.s)
B.bsa=new A.K(B.atz,"The Prophet \ufdfa taught: \"Allahumma akfini bi halalika 'an haramika, wa aghnini bi fadlika 'amman siwaka\" (O Allah, suffice me with what You have made lawful against what You have made forbidden, and enrich me with Your bounty beyond anyone else). (Sunan al-Tirmidhi 3563, hasan per Darussalam).")
B.aA3=s(["dua for marriage","spouse dua","husband dua","wife dua"],t.s)
B.brb=new A.K(B.aA3,"Allah describes His servants as those who say: \"Rabbana hab lana min azwajina wa dhurriyyatina qurrata a'yunin wa-j'alna lil-muttaqina imama\" (Our Lord, grant us from among our wives and offspring comfort to our eyes and make us an example for the righteous). (Qur'an 25:74).")
B.aA8=s(["dua for children","child dua","baby dua","pregnancy dua"],t.s)
B.bqB=new A.K(B.aA8,"Faith is a gift to ask for: Allah says He has endeared the faith to the believers and made disbelief, defiance and disobedience hateful to them (Qur'an 49:7) - so ask Him to keep it so. For pregnancy: \"Rabbi hab li min ladunka dhurriyyatan tayyibah\" (My Lord, grant me from Yourself a good offspring). (Qur'an 3:38).")
B.aCf=s(["dua for health","sickness dua","healing dua","shifa"],t.s)
B.bmr=new A.K(B.aCf,"The Prophet \ufdfa said that if someone visits a sick person whose time has not yet come and says seven times a supplication asking Allah, the Mighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to cure him, Allah will relieve him of that illness (Sunan Abi Dawud 3106, sahih per al-Albani).")
B.aEL=s(["dua for protection","protection dua","safe dua"],t.s)
B.bmI=new A.K(B.aEL,"The Prophet \ufdfa said: \"Whoever says three times every morning and evening: Bismillahi alladhi la yadurru ma'asmihi shay'un fi al-ardi wa la fi al-sama'i, wa huwa al-sami'u al-'alim \u2014 In the name of Allah, with whose name nothing on earth or in heaven can cause harm, and He is the All-Hearing, All-Knowing \u2014 nothing will harm him.\" (Sunan al-Tirmidhi 3388, hasan per Darussalam).")
B.aNC=s(["dua for exam","test dua","study dua","knowledge dua"],t.s)
B.bq_=new A.K(B.aNC,"Before an exam, begin with Bismillah, ask Allah for ease, and study as well as you can: trusting Allah does not replace preparing. The Qur'an gives a short du'a to ask for knowledge: \"My Lord, increase me in knowledge.\" (Qur'an 20:114).")
B.aCe=s(["dua for distress","hardship dua","difficulty dua"],t.s)
B.bpa=new A.K(B.aCe,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "The supplication of Dhun-Nun (Yunus) when he supplicated while in the belly of the whale: La ilaha illa anta, subhanaka, inni kuntu min al-zalimin \u2014 There is no god but You, glory be to You, indeed I was among the wrongdoers. No Muslim supplicates with it for anything but Allah answers him." (Sunan al-Tirmidhi 3505, sahih per Darussalam).')
B.aBT=s(["dua for debt","loan dua","owe money dua"],t.s)
B.bq1=new A.K(B.aBT,"The Prophet \ufdfa said: \"Whoever is burdened with debt and says: Allahumma akfini bi halalika 'an haramika, wa aghnini bi fadlika 'amman siwaka \u2014 O Allah, suffice me with Your lawful against Your forbidden, and enrich me with Your bounty beyond anyone else \u2014 Allah will suffice him.\" (Sunan al-Tirmidhi 3563, hasan per Darussalam).")
B.azV=s(["dua for righteous death","good death","husn al-khatimah"],t.s)
B.bmB=new A.K(B.azV,"The Prophet \ufdfa said: \"When you finish the obligatory prayer, say: Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min al-jubni wa al-bukhl, wa a'udhu bika min an uradda ila ardhal al-'umur, wa a'udhu bika min fitnat al-dunya wa fitnat al-qabr wa fitnat al-masih al-dajjal.\" (Sahih Muslim 588). Also seek: \"Allahumma inni as'aluka husn al-khatimah\" (O Allah, I ask You for a good ending).")
B.aDL=s(["dua entering masjid","masjid entrance","mosque dua"],t.s)
B.bnW=new A.K(B.aDL,'When entering the masjid, say: "Allahumma ftah li abwaba rahmatik" (O Allah, open for me the doors of Your mercy). When leaving, say: "Allahumma inni as\'aluka min fadlik" (O Allah, I ask You from Your bounty). (Sahih Muslim 713).')
B.avA=s(["dua for parents","father dua","mother dua","parents forgiveness"],t.s)
B.brB=new A.K(B.avA,'Allah says: "And lower to them the wing of humility out of mercy and say: My Lord, have mercy upon them as they brought me up when I was small." (Qur\'an 17:24). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "The pleasure of the Lord is in the pleasure of the parent, and the displeasure of the Lord is in the displeasure of the parent." (Sunan al-Tirmidhi 1899, hasan per al-Tirmidhi).')
B.aL5=s(["dua for forgiveness","istighfar","seek forgiveness","sin"],t.s)
B.brQ=new A.K(B.aL5,"The Prophet \ufdfa said: \"The most superior way of asking for forgiveness is to say: Allahumma anta rabbi, la ilaha illa anta, khalaqtani wa ana 'abduka, wa ana 'ala ahdika wa wa'dika mastata'tu, a'udhu bika min sharri ma sana'tu, abu'u laka bi ni'matika 'alayya, wa abu'u laka bi dhanbi, fa ighfir li, fa innahu la yaghfiru al-dhunuba illa anta.\" (O Allah, You are my Lord. There is no god but You. You created me, and I am Your servant, and I am faithful to my covenant and promise to You as best I can. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your blessings upon me, and I acknowledge my sin. So forgive me, for none forgives sins but You.) (Sahih al-Bukhari 6306).")
B.arS=s(["what is halal","what is haram","halal and haram","meaning of halal","meaning of haram"],t.s)
B.bol=new A.K(B.arS,'Allah says: "He has only forbidden to you dead animals, blood, the flesh of swine, and that which has been dedicated to other than Allah." (Qur\'an 2:173). Scholars state the general principle: what Allah has made lawful is halal, what He has forbidden is haram, and what He has not addressed is generally permitted. For a specific question, ask a qualified scholar.')
B.aGH=s(["fard","obligatory","wajib","mandatory"],t.s)
B.bnz=new A.K(B.aGH,'Fard (obligatory) acts are those for which there is definitive evidence in the Qur\'an or mutawatir hadith. Neglecting them is sinful. Examples: the five daily prayers, fasting Ramadan, zakat, Hajj. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no god but Allah and Muhammad is His Messenger, establishing prayer, giving zakat, fasting Ramadan, and performing Hajj." (Sahih al-Bukhari 8, Sahih Muslim 16).')
B.avM=s(["sunnah","mustahabb","recommended","nafl","voluntary"],t.s)
B.bnY=new A.K(B.avM,"Sunnah acts are those the Prophet \ufdfa regularly performed and encouraged. They are divided into: Sunnah muakkadah (emphasized, like the two rak'ahs before Fajr) and Sunnah ghayr muakkadah (non-emphasized).")
B.aJU=s(["makruh","disliked","discouraged"],t.s)
B.bmO=new A.K(B.aJU,"Makruh (disliked) acts are those for which there is evidence of discouragement but not prohibition. Examples: eating with the left hand, wasting water during wudu, praying after Asr until sunset.")
B.aEW=s(["bidah","innovation","biddah"],t.s)
B.boD=new A.K(B.aEW,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Whoever introduces into this matter of ours (Islam) something that is not part of it, it will be rejected." (Sahih al-Bukhari 2697, Sahih Muslim 1718). Bidah is any newly invented matter in religion that has no basis in the Qur\'an or authentic Sunnah. However, worldly innovations (technology, medicine) are not bidah.')
B.aBH=s(["shirk","associating partners","polytheism"],t.s)
B.brh=new A.K(B.aBH,'Allah says: "Indeed, Allah does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills." (Qur\'an 4:48). Shirk is the greatest sin \u2014 associating partners with Allah in worship, lordship, or names/attributes. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Shall I not inform you of the greatest of major sins? They are: associating partners with Allah, disobeying parents, and bearing false testimony." (Sahih al-Bukhari 2654, Sahih Muslim 87).')
B.auq=s(["tawbah","repentance","turning back"],t.s)
B.bmY=new A.K(B.auq,'Allah says: "Say, O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins. Indeed, it is He who is the Forgiving, the Merciful." (Qur\'an 39:53). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Allah is more delighted with the repentance of His servant than one of you who finds his lost camel." (Sahih al-Bukhari 6309, Sahih Muslim 2747).')
B.as0=s(["tawakkul","trust in allah","reliance"],t.s)
B.bsh=new A.K(B.as0,'Allah says: "And whoever relies upon Allah \u2014 then He is sufficient for him." (Qur\'an 65:3). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "If you had relied upon Allah with true reliance, He would have provided for you as He provides for the bird: it goes out hungry in the morning and returns full in the evening." (Sunan al-Tirmidhi 2344, hasan per Darussalam).')
B.aNd=s(["ikhlas","sincerity","pure intention"],t.s)
B.brI=new A.K(B.aNd,'Allah says: "And they were not commanded except to worship Allah, being sincere to Him in religion, inclining to truth." (Qur\'an 98:5). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Actions are but by intentions, and every person will have what he intended." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1, Sahih Muslim 1907). Ikhlas is doing everything solely for Allah\'s pleasure.')
B.aI6=s(["ihsan","excellence","perfection"],t.s)
B.bpA=new A.K(B.aI6,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Ihsan is to worship Allah as if you see Him, and if you do not see Him, then indeed He sees you." (Sahih al-Bukhari 50, Sahih Muslim 8). Ihsan is the highest level of faith \u2014 excellence in every action, knowing Allah is always watching.')
B.aAK=s(["marriage","nikah","getting married","wedding"],t.s)
B.boi=new A.K(B.aAK,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Marriage is part of my sunnah, and whoever does not follow my sunnah is not of me." (Sunan Ibn Majah 1846, hasan per Darussalam). The essential conditions are: offer and acceptance, mahr (dowry), two witnesses, and the wali (guardian) for the bride.')
B.ayf=s(["mahr","dowry","bride price"],t.s)
B.bsm=new A.K(B.ayf,"Allah says: \"And give the women [upon marriage] their [bridal] gifts graciously.\" (Qur'an 4:4). The mahr is the husband's gift to the wife, which becomes her exclusive property. Scholars encourage keeping it modest and easy, so that marriage is not made hard.")
B.aKb=s(["walima","wedding feast","marriage banquet"],t.s)
B.bpO=new A.K(B.aKb,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "The worst of food is the food of a walima to which the rich are invited and the poor are left out. And whoever does not respond to the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger." (Sahih al-Bukhari 5173, Sahih Muslim 1429). The walima is a sunnah strongly encouraged on the day of marriage or within three days.')
B.aKt=s(["divorce","talaq","ending marriage"],t.s)
B.brV=new A.K(B.aKt,'Allah says: "Divorce is twice. Then, either keep her in an acceptable manner or release her with good treatment." (Qur\'an 2:229). Divorce is permitted but widely regarded as a last resort, after reconciliation has been tried. It must be pronounced clearly during a period of purity (not menstruation) without intimacy.')
B.aAi=s(["rights of wife","wife rights","husband duties"],t.s)
B.bqF=new A.K(B.aAi,'The Prophet \ufdfa said in his farewell sermon: "Fear Allah concerning women. Indeed, you have taken them under Allah\'s trust, and their private parts are lawful to you by the word of Allah." (Sahih Muslim 1218). Rights include: mahr, maintenance (food, clothing, housing), kind treatment, and not harming physically or emotionally.')
B.aAj=s(["rights of husband","husband rights","wife duties"],t.s)
B.bou=new A.K(B.aAj,"There are well-known teachings about a wife's rights and duties toward her husband that this app has not checked, so it does not quote them. Rights are mutual; the usual summary includes obedience in permissible matters, protection of honor, and managing the household - ask a scholar of your madhhab for specifics.")
B.aK5=s(["child rights","children rights","raising children"],t.s)
B.bnC=new A.K(B.aK5,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Each of you is a shepherd and each of you is responsible for his flock. The man is a shepherd over his household and he is responsible for them." (Sahih al-Bukhari 893, Sahih Muslim 1829). Children have rights: good name, proper upbringing, education, affection, and fair treatment between siblings.')
B.aoJ=s(["breastfeeding","nursing","infant feeding"],t.s)
B.bpd=new A.K(B.aoJ,'Allah says: "Mothers may breastfeed their children two complete years for whoever wishes to complete the nursing period." (Qur\'an 2:233). Nursing also creates family ties: among those a person may not marry Allah lists "your [milk] mothers who nursed you, your sisters through nursing" (Qur\'an 4:23). For the details of foster-nursing rulings, ask a scholar.')
B.aHP=s(["circumcision","khitan","sunan al-fitrah"],t.s)
B.bn0=new A.K(B.aHP,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Five are from the fitrah: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, trimming the mustache, cutting the nails, and plucking the armpit hair." (Sahih al-Bukhari 5889, Sahih Muslim 257). Circumcision is obligatory for men and recommended for women (according to the majority view).')
B.awk=s(["aqiqah","newborn sacrifice","baby sacrifice"],t.s)
B.bq8=new A.K(B.awk,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Every child is held in pledge for his aqiqah, which is sacrificed for him on his seventh day, and he is named on his seventh day, and his head is shaved." (Sunan Abi Dawud 2838, sahih per al-Albani). Two sheep for a boy and one for a girl.')
B.avc=s(["zakat","zakah","alms","charity obligation"],t.s)
B.bmN=new A.K(B.avc,'Allah says: "And establish prayer and give zakah." (Qur\'an 2:110). Zakat is 2.5% of wealth held for one lunar year above the nisab (threshold: the value of 595 g of silver or 85 g of gold \u2014 the Zakat calculator shows today\'s figure). It is due on gold, silver, cash, trade goods, and livestock. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Whoever is made wealthy by Allah and does not pay its zakat, his wealth will be made into a bald snake on the Day of Resurrection." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1403).')
B.aqd=s(["zakat calculation","how to calculate zakat","nisab"],t.s)
B.boX=new A.K(B.aqd,'Zakat is due when wealth reaches the nisab (85g of gold or 595g of silver) and is held for one lunar year. Rate: 2.5% on cash, gold, silver, and trade goods. Agricultural produce: 5% (irrigated) or 10% (rain-fed). Livestock varies by number. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "There is no zakat on less than five camels, less than five awaq of silver, and less than five wasaq of dates." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1447).')
B.aEA=s(["sadaqah","voluntary charity","giving"],t.s)
B.bmF=new A.K(B.aEA,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Charity does not decrease wealth. No one forgives another except that Allah increases him in honor. And no one humbles himself for Allah except that Allah raises him." (Sahih Muslim 2588). Sadaqah can be money, food, a smile, removing harm from the road, or even a kind word.')
B.aqk=s(["riba","interest","usury","bank interest"],t.s)
B.bpc=new A.K(B.aqk,'Allah says: "But Allah has permitted trade and has forbidden interest." (Qur\'an 2:275). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Allah has cursed the one who consumes riba, the one who gives it, the one who records it, and the two witnesses to it." (Sahih Muslim 1598). Conventional bank interest on savings and loans is riba and forbidden.')
B.aMK=s(["stocks","shares","investment","halal investing"],t.s)
B.br8=new A.K(B.aMK,'Whether a particular stock is permissible depends on what the company does, how it is financed and where its income comes from, and scholars set the limits differently, so I will not give you a number or a verdict. Allah says: "But Allah has permitted trade and has forbidden interest." (Qur\'an 2:275), and intoxicants and gambling are called defilement from the work of Satan (Qur\'an 5:90), so a business built on those is to be avoided. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "The upper hand is better than the lower hand." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1427). For your own money, please ask a scholar or a Shariah screening service you trust.')
B.aJo=s(["insurance","life insurance","halal insurance"],t.s)
B.bsd=new A.K(B.aJo,"Scholars have discussed insurance under the headings of riba (interest), gharar (excessive uncertainty) and maysir (gambling), and they differ on how those apply to different kinds of cover. Takaful (Islamic cooperative insurance), based on donation and mutual assistance, was developed as an alternative. I have no verified text on my shelf that settles a ruling, so for a real decision please ask a qualified scholar.")
B.aqa=s(["inheritance","mirath","wasiyyah","islamic will","writing a will"],t.s)
B.bov=new A.K(B.aqa,'Allah says: "Allah instructs you concerning your children: for the male, what is equal to the share of two females." (Qur\'an 4:11). Islamic inheritance is obligatory (fard) and cannot be willed away. Only up to one-third can be bequeathed to non-heirs, and scholars hold that a bequest is not made to someone who is already an heir, since their share is fixed.')
B.aon=s(["burial","burying dead","grave","kafan"],t.s)
B.brm=new A.K(B.aon,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Hasten the funeral. If the deceased was righteous, you are advancing him toward good. If otherwise, you are putting evil off your necks." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1315, Sahih Muslim 944). The body is washed, shrouded in white cloth (kafan), prayed over, and buried facing the qiblah.')
B.axJ=s(["visiting graves","graveyard","cemetery"],t.s)
B.brD=new A.K(B.axJ,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "I used to forbid you from visiting graves, but now visit them, for they remind you of the Hereafter." (Sahih Muslim 977). When visiting, greet the deceased with peace, make dua for them, and reflect on death.')
B.aHx=s(["dua for deceased","dead person dua","funeral dua"],t.s)
B.brE=new A.K(B.aHx,'The Prophet \ufdfa taught: "Allahumma ighfir li hayyina wa mayyitina, wa shahidina wa gha\'ibina, wa saghirina wa kabirina, wa dhakarina wa unthana" (O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our young and our old, our males and our females). (Sunan Abi Dawud 3201, sahih per al-Albani).')
B.asd=s(["barzakh","grave life","punishment of grave"],t.s)
B.bnf=new A.K(B.asd,"The grave is regarded as the first stage of the Hereafter. The soul experiences questioning by Munkar and Nakir, and either comfort or punishment, according to the creed of Ahl as-Sunnah.")
B.aOP=s(["day of judgment","qiyamah","last day","resurrection"],t.s)
B.bqc=new A.K(B.aOP,'Allah says: "The Day every soul will find what it has done of good present [before it] and what it has done of evil." (Qur\'an 3:30). Scholars remind us that prayer is the first deed a person is accountable for, which is why guarding it matters.')
B.aIz=s(["jannah","paradise","heaven"],t.s)
B.bmZ=new A.K(B.aIz,'Allah says: "And no soul knows what has been hidden for them of comfort for eyes as reward for what they used to do." (Qur\'an 32:17). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Allah says: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no heart has imagined." (Sahih al-Bukhari 3244, Sahih Muslim 2824).')
B.aIy=s(["jahannam","hellfire","hell","nar"],t.s)
B.bor=new A.K(B.aIy,'Allah says: "Indeed, Hell has been lying in wait for the transgressors." (Qur\'an 78:21-22). The Prophet \ufdfa said that a stone thrown into Hell seventy years ago was still falling until it only now reached the bottom. (Sahih Muslim 2844).')
B.aFG=s(["depression","sad","hopeless","empty"],t.s)
B.bqq=new A.K(B.aFG,'Allah says: "And We will surely test you with something of fear and hunger and a loss of wealth and lives and fruits, but give good tidings to the patient." (Qur\'an 2:155). The Prophet \ufdfa experienced deep grief \u2014 he wept for Ibrahim, he lost Khadijah and Abu Talib in the same year. Depression is not a lack of faith; it is a test. Seek help: medical, spiritual, and communal.')
B.aLs=s(["loneliness","alone","no friends","isolated"],t.s)
B.bqU=new A.K(B.aLs,'Allah says: "And He is with you wherever you are." (Qur\'an 57:4). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Allah says: I am as My servant thinks of Me. I am with him when he remembers Me." (Sahih al-Bukhari 7405, Sahih Muslim 2675). Loneliness is real, but you are never truly alone. The One who created you is closer than your jugular vein.')
B.aof=s(["betrayal","cheated","lied to","backstabbed"],t.s)
B.bq9=new A.K(B.aof,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "There are three signs of a hypocrite: when he speaks, he lies; when he makes a promise, he breaks it; and when he is entrusted, he betrays." (Sahih al-Bukhari 33, Sahih Muslim 59). If you have been betrayed, know that the Prophet \ufdfa was betrayed by his own uncle and tribe. Your pain is understood.')
B.aEt=s(["anger","mad","furious","rage"],t.s)
B.br7=new A.K(B.aEt,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "The strong is not the one who overcomes people by his strength, but the strong is the one who controls himself while in anger." (Sahih al-Bukhari 6114, Sahih Muslim 2609). When angry, sit down if standing, lie down if sitting, and make wudu \u2014 the physical change breaks the emotional spiral.')
B.aJx=s(["laziness","procrastination","can't start","unmotivated"],t.s)
B.bsk=new A.K(B.aJx,'Allah says: "So when you have finished [your duties], then stand up [for worship]. And to your Lord direct [your] longing." (Qur\'an 94:7-8). The Prophet \ufdfa sought refuge from laziness: "Allahumma inni a\'udhu bika min al-\'ajzi wa al-kasal" (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity and laziness). (Sahih al-Bukhari 6369).')
B.aGJ=s(["fear","scared","afraid","terror"],t.s)
B.bpB=new A.K(B.aGJ,'Allah says: "Fear not. Indeed, I am with you both; I hear and I see." (Qur\'an 20:46). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Allah says: I am as My servant expects of Me." (Sahih al-Bukhari 7405, Sahih Muslim 2675). Say Hasbunallahu wa ni\'mal wakeel (Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best Disposer of affairs) \u2014 the same words Ibrahim said when thrown into the fire.')
B.aHn=s(["guilt","ashamed","regret","remorse"],t.s)
B.bmt=new A.K(B.aHn,'Allah says: "Say, O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins." (Qur\'an 39:53). Guilt that leads to repentance is from Allah. Guilt that leads to despair is from Shaytan. The door of tawbah is open until the soul reaches the throat.')
B.aIs=s(["envy","jealous","hasad","evil eye"],t.s)
B.bpp=new A.K(B.aIs,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "The evil eye is real." (Sahih al-Bukhari 5740, Sahih Muslim 2187). Protect yourself with: (1) regular adhkar, (2) reciting the last three surahs morning and evening, (3) saying "MashaAllah, la quwwata illa billah" when admiring something. If you feel envy, make dua for the person \u2014 it transforms the poison into prayer.')
B.ayy=s(["nightmares","bad dreams","scary dream"],t.s)
B.bpZ=new A.K(B.ayy,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Dreams are of three types: from Allah, from Shaytan, and from the self. If one of you sees something he dislikes, let him spit dryly to his left three times and seek refuge in Allah from its evil, and it will not harm him." (Sahih Muslim 2261). Do not tell others about bad dreams.')
B.aKK=s(["ocd","waswasa","whispers","doubts"],t.s)
B.brC=new A.K(B.aKK,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "The Shaytan comes to one of you and says: Who created this? Who created that? Until he says: Who created your Lord? When that happens, let him seek refuge in Allah and stop." (Sahih al-Bukhari 3276, Sahih Muslim 134). Waswasa about wudu and prayer is from Shaytan. Do not repeat acts beyond three times.')
B.aJ0=s(["laylatul qadr","night of decree","power night"],t.s)
B.bo6=new A.K(B.aJ0,'Allah says: "Indeed, We sent the Qur\'an down during the Night of Decree. And what can make you know what is the Night of Decree? The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months." (Qur\'an 97:1-3). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Seek it in the last ten nights, on the odd nights." (Sahih al-Bukhari 2017, Sahih Muslim 1169).')
B.aDD=s(["itikaf","spiritual retreat","mosque retreat"],t.s)
B.bmM=new A.K(B.aDD,"The Prophet \ufdfa used to perform i'tikaf (spiritual retreat) in the last ten days of Ramadan (Sahih al-Bukhari 2025, Sahih Muslim 1172). It involves staying in the masjid with the intention of worship, abstaining from sins, and increasing in Quran, dhikr, and dua.")
B.aF0=s(["zakat ul fitr","fitrana","eid charity"],t.s)
B.boV=new A.K(B.aF0,"Zakat al-fitr (fitrana) is obligatory on every Muslim who has more than their needs: about one sa' (roughly 2.5kg) of a staple food such as dates, barley, wheat, or raisins, or its monetary equivalent in the view of many scholars. It must be given before the Eid prayer. It purifies the fast from lapses and feeds the poor.")
B.ax8=s(["breaking fast","iftar","opening fast"],t.s)
B.bpl=new A.K(B.ax8,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "The people will remain upon goodness as long as they hasten to break the fast." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1957, Sahih Muslim 1098). Break with dates and water, saying: "Dhahaba al-zama\'u wa abtalat al-\'uruq wa thabata al-ajru inshaAllah" (The thirst is gone, the veins are moistened, and the reward is confirmed, if Allah wills).')
B.bo3=new A.K(B.F4,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Eat suhoor, for in suhoor there is blessing." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1923, Sahih Muslim 1095). The best time is the last third of the night. Delay it as close to Fajr as possible without risking eating after the adhan.')
B.aJ3=s(["kaffarah","kaffara","fast expiation","expiation for breaking the fast","kaffarah for breaking the fast","kaffarah for breaking fast"],t.s)
B.bsn=new A.K(B.aJ3,"The kaffarah (expiation) in the hadith of Sahih al-Bukhari 1936 is for a man who deliberately had intercourse during a day of Ramadan: he was told to free a slave, or fast two consecutive months, or feed sixty poor people. For anything else, such as vomiting, forgetting, or eating by mistake, I have no verified text on my shelf, so I will not guess. Please ask a qualified scholar about your own case.\n[GO:/sources]")
B.aFO=s(["vomit","vomiting","throw up","threw up","puke"],t.s)
B.bqa=new A.K(B.aFO,"Whether vomiting affects the fast depends on details, for example whether it came on its own or was brought on, and scholars discuss those details. I do not have a verified text on my shelf for it, so I will not guess, and I will not call it expiation or no expiation. Please ask a qualified scholar; Our Sources lists one.\n[GO:/sources]")
B.aK4=s(["music","singing","nasheed","songs"],t.s)
B.bq2=new A.K(B.aK4,'Scholars have differed on music and instruments for centuries. One report often cited is: "From among my Ummah there will be people who will consider zina, silk, alcohol, and musical instruments as lawful." (Sahih al-Bukhari 5590), and scholars discuss how it applies. I have no verified text on my shelf that settles it, so please ask a scholar you trust.')
B.aI7=s(["images","photos","pictures","drawing"],t.s)
B.bpr=new A.K(B.aI7,"The Prophet \ufdfa said that the makers of images will receive the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection (Sahih al-Bukhari 5954, Sahih Muslim 2109). Photography of living beings is a matter of scholarly difference. The majority of contemporary scholars permit it for necessity (ID, education, journalism).")
B.arJ=s(["dogs","pet dog","keeping dog"],t.s)
B.bpN=new A.K(B.arJ,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Whoever keeps a dog, except a dog for hunting, farming, or herding livestock, will have his reward deducted by two qirats every day." (Sahih al-Bukhari 2322, Sahih Muslim 1574). Dogs are not impure themselves, but their saliva requires washing (seven times, one with soil).')
B.apf=s(["gold silk men","men wear gold","men silk"],t.s)
B.brc=new A.K(B.apf,"Scholars agree that gold is forbidden for men and permitted for women, and that pure silk is likewise forbidden for men. Men may not wear gold rings, chains, or clothing with silk. Women may wear both.")
B.awl=s(["beard","shave beard","trim beard"],t.s)
B.bq6=new A.K(B.awl,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Trim the mustaches and leave the beard." (Sahih Muslim 259). The majority of scholars consider growing the beard obligatory for men and shaving it sinful. Trimming it shorter than a fistful is also discouraged.')
B.aKz=s(["siwak","miswak","tooth stick"],t.s)
B.bph=new A.K(B.aKz,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "If I did not fear hardship for my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwak with every prayer." (Sahih al-Bukhari 887, Sahih Muslim 252). It is a strongly recommended sunnah before every prayer, before reading Quran, and upon entering home.')
B.aoK=s(["tajweed","quran recitation","pronunciation"],t.s)
B.br_=new A.K(B.aoK,"The Prophet \ufdfa said: \"The one who is proficient in the recitation of the Qur'an will be with the honorable and obedient scribes (angels), and he who recites the Qur'an and finds it difficult to recite, doing his best to recite it in the best way possible, will have a double reward.\" (Sahih al-Bukhari 4937, Sahih Muslim 798).")
B.ay8=s(["memorize quran","hifz","memorization"],t.s)
B.boQ=new A.K(B.ay8,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "The best of you are those who learn the Qur\'an and teach it." (Sahih al-Bukhari 5027). For memorization: (1) read with understanding, (2) repeat each ayah 10 times, (3) connect ayahs, (4) review daily, (5) recite in prayer.')
B.arq=s(["quran adab","quran manners","reading quran"],t.s)
B.bon=new A.K(B.arq,"When reading the Qur'an: be in a state of wudu, face the qiblah if possible, begin with ta'awwudh (a'udhu billahi min al-shaytan al-rajim), read with tartil (measured recitation), and weep or try to weep. The Prophet \ufdfa said: \"Recite the Qur'an, for on the Day of Resurrection it will come as an intercessor for its companions.\" (Sahih Muslim 804).")
B.aLS=s(["ayat al kursi","throne verse","greatest verse"],t.s)
B.boN=new A.K(B.aLS,"Scholars encourage reciting Ayat al-Kursi at the end of every obligatory prayer. It is regarded as the greatest verse of the Qur'an (Qur'an 2:255), containing the greatest name of Allah.")
B.aHe=s(["surah ikhlas","surah falaq","surah nas","muawwidhat"],t.s)
B.bnl=new A.K(B.aHe,"Each night before sleeping the Prophet \ufdfa recited Al-Ikhlas, Al-Falaq and An-Nas into his cupped hands, blew into them and wiped over his body (Sahih al-Bukhari 5017). These three surahs are called al-Mu'awwidhat, and many Muslims recite them morning and evening for protection.")
B.azK=s(["last two ayahs baqarah","baqarah end","amana rasul"],t.s)
B.bmC=new A.K(B.azK,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Whoever recites the last two verses of Surah al-Baqarah at night, they will suffice him." (Sahih al-Bukhari 4008, Sahih Muslim 808).')
B.aLK=s(["dua after adhan","adhan response","call to prayer"],t.s)
B.bnE=new A.K(B.aLK,'When the mu\'adhin says "Hayya \'ala al-salah" and "Hayya \'ala al-falah," say: "La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah." After the adhan, send blessings on the Prophet and say: "Allahumma rabba hadhihi al-da\'wati al-tammah, wa al-salati al-qaimah, ati Muhammadan al-wasilata wa al-fadilah, wa b\'athhu maqaman mahmudan alladhi wa\'adtahu." (Sahih al-Bukhari 614, Sahih Muslim 384).')
B.aA1=s(["dua between sajdas","sujood","prostration"],t.s)
B.bmL=new A.K(B.aA1,'In sujood, say: "Subhana rabbiy al-a\'la" (Glory be to my Lord, the Most High) at least three times. Between the two sajdas, say: "Rabbi ighfir li, warhamni, wahdini, wa \'afini, warzuqni" (My Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me well-being, and provide for me). (Sunan Abi Dawud).')
B.aMB=s(["tasbih","subhanallah","glorification"],t.s)
B.bpI=new A.K(B.aMB,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Is one of you unable to earn a thousand hasanat every day?" They said: How? He said: "Say SubhanAllah one hundred times, and a thousand hasanat are written for him, or a thousand sins are removed." (Sahih Muslim 2698).')
B.aMx=s(["tahmid","alhamdulillah","praise"],t.s)
B.br6=new A.K(B.aMx,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Alhamdulillah fills the scale." (Sahih Muslim 223). Saying it after every blessing \u2014 a meal, safety, health \u2014 is the sign of a grateful heart. Allah says: "If you are grateful, I will surely increase you." (Qur\'an 14:7).')
B.aFR=s(["takbir","allahu akbar","magnification"],t.s)
B.bnj=new A.K(B.aFR,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "For me to say SubhanAllah, walhamdulillah, wa la ilaha illa Allah, wa Allahu akbar is more beloved to me than everything the sun rises upon." (Sahih Muslim 2137). These four phrases are the best dhikr and are called the tasbihat.')
B.aJD=s(["tahlil","la ilaha illallah","oneness"],t.s)
B.bo0=new A.K(B.aJD,"La ilaha illa Allah is the word of tawhid, the first pillar of Islam and the heart of all dhikr. Say it often, with understanding and sincerity.")
B.aB0=s(["salawat","durud","blessings on prophet"],t.s)
B.bpb=new A.K(B.aB0,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Whoever sends blessings upon me once, Allah will send blessings upon him ten times." (Sahih Muslim 408). The minimum is "Allahumma salli \'ala Muhammad wa \'ala ali Muhammad." It is said in tashahhud, after adhan, when hearing his name, and in times of distress.')
B.azM=s(["morning adhkar","evening adhkar","daily adhkar"],t.s)
B.bnu=new A.K(B.azM,"The Prophet \ufdfa said: \"Whoever says in the morning and evening: Bismillahi alladhi la yadurru ma'asmihi shay'un fi al-ardi wa la fi al-sama'i, wa huwa al-sami'u al-'alim \u2014 three times \u2014 nothing will harm him that day or night.\" (Sunan al-Tirmidhi 3388, hasan per Darussalam).")
B.aOT=s(["hajj","pilgrimage","fifth pillar"],t.s)
B.bpX=new A.K(B.aOT,'Allah says: "And [due] to Allah from the people is a pilgrimage to the House - for whoever is able to find thereto a way." (Qur\'an 3:97). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Whoever performs Hajj and does not commit any obscenity or transgression, he returns as the day his mother bore him." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1521, Sahih Muslim 1350).')
B.aCs=s(["umrah","minor pilgrimage","lesser pilgrimage"],t.s)
B.boc=new A.K(B.aCs,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Umrah is an expiation for what comes between it and the previous Umrah." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1773, Sahih Muslim 1349). It can be performed any time of year and consists of: ihram, tawaf, sa\'i, and shaving or trimming the hair.')
B.aEN=s(["ihram","pilgrimage state","hajj clothes"],t.s)
B.bnT=new A.K(B.aEN,"Ihram is the sacred state entered before Hajj or Umrah. For men: two unstitched white cloths. For women: any modest clothing. Prohibitions in ihram: cutting hair or nails, wearing perfume, hunting, marital relations, and arguing. The standing at Arafah is the essential rite of Hajj: there is no Hajj without it.")
B.aMD=s(["tawaf","circumambulation","kaaba"],t.s)
B.bpV=new A.K(B.aMD,"Tawaf is circling the Kaaba seven times, starting from the Black Stone, with the Kaaba on the left. At each circuit pilgrims touch or kiss the Black Stone if they can, or point to it from a distance.")
B.aFb=s(["saee","safa marwa","running"],t.s)
B.bmU=new A.K(B.aFb,"Sa'i is walking seven times between Safa and Marwa, commemorating Hajar's search for water for Ismail. The Prophet \ufdfa said that had she left the water alone, it would have flowed on the surface of the earth (Sahih al-Bukhari 3365).")
B.aMd=s(["ruqyah","healing verses","spiritual healing"],t.s)
B.bnU=new A.K(B.aMd,"Each night before sleeping the Prophet \ufdfa recited Al-Ikhlas, Al-Falaq and An-Nas into his cupped hands, blew into them and wiped over his body (Sahih al-Bukhari 5017). Ruqyah is permissible if: (1) using Allah's words or His names, (2) in Arabic or a language understood, (3) believing the cure is from Allah alone.")
B.aBL=s(["black magic","sihr","witchcraft"],t.s)
B.bqT=new A.K(B.aBL,'Allah says: "And from the evil of the blowers in knots." (Qur\'an 113:4). The Prophet \ufdfa was affected by magic (Sahih al-Bukhari 3268, Sahih Muslim 2189). Treatment: (1) regular adhkar, (2) ruqyah, (3) medical evaluation for physical symptoms.')
B.aIG=s(["jinn","shaytan","devil","satan"],t.s)
B.brd=new A.K(B.aIG,'Allah says: "Indeed, Satan is an enemy to you; so take him as an enemy." (Qur\'an 35:6). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Satan runs through the son of Adam like blood runs through his veins." (Sahih al-Bukhari 3281, Sahih Muslim 2174). Protection: regular adhkar, seeking refuge before entering home and before eating, and avoiding sin.')
B.aJL=s(["hasad","evil eye","ayn","nazar"],t.s)
B.bqe=new A.K(B.aJL,'The Prophet \ufdfa said the evil eye is real (Sahih Muslim 2188). Common practices, which are advice rather than a ruling: (1) conceal blessings when possible, (2) say "MashaAllah, la quwwata illa billah," (3) recite the three Quls morning and evening, (4) ruqyah for the affected.')
B.avP=s(["salah on time","prayer punctuality","pray on time"],t.s)
B.bo1=new A.K(B.avP,'Allah says: "Indeed, prayer has been decreed upon the believers a decree of specified times." (Qur\'an 4:103). Praying on time matters because prayer is the first deed a person is accountable for.')
B.azu=s(["congregation","jamaah","praying together","group prayer"],t.s)
B.bs5=new A.K(B.azu,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Prayer in congregation is twenty-seven times better than prayer alone." (Sahih al-Bukhari 645, Sahih Muslim 650). For men, it is strongly emphasized to pray in the masjid. For women, praying at home is better but the masjid is permitted.')
B.auo=s(["women prayer","women masjid","ladies prayer"],t.s)
B.brY=new A.K(B.auo,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah." (Sahih al-Bukhari 900, Sahih Muslim 442). Women have full right to attend the masjid, though praying at home is considered better for them. They should dress modestly and avoid perfume.')
B.aK_=s(["menstruation","period","menses","hayd"],t.s)
B.bmp=new A.K(B.aK_,'Allah says: "They ask you about menstruation. Say: It is harm, so keep away from wives during menstruation." (Qur\'an 2:222). A menstruating woman does not pray or fast (Sahih al-Bukhari 304); scholars differ on touching the Qur\'an and entering the masjid - ask a scholar. She makes up missed fasts but not prayers. The Prophet \ufdfa said to Aisha when her period came: "This is something Allah has decreed for the daughters of Adam." (Sahih al-Bukhari 294).')
B.aoF=s(["postpartum","nifas","bleeding after birth"],t.s)
B.br9=new A.K(B.aoF,"Postpartum bleeding (nifas) lasts up to forty days. The woman does not pray or fast during this period. After forty days, if bleeding continues, it is considered istihadha (irregular bleeding) and she performs wudu for each prayer. (Fiqh consensus based on Sahih al-Bukhari and Sahih Muslim).")
B.aou=s(["istihadha","irregular bleeding","spotting"],t.s)
B.boa=new A.K(B.aou,"Istihadha is bleeding outside the normal menstrual cycle. The woman performs wudu for each prayer time and prays. The Prophet \ufdfa told Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh that her bleeding was from a vein and not menstruation: pause the prayer for the days of her real period, then wash off the blood and pray. (Sahih al-Bukhari 228).")
B.avs=s(["neighbors","rights of neighbor","neighbor rights"],t.s)
B.bnd=new A.K(B.avs,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Jibril kept advising me to treat neighbors well until I thought he would make them heirs." (Sahih al-Bukhari 6014, Sahih Muslim 2625). Rights include: greeting, helping in need, protecting their honor, not harming them with noise or smell, and sharing food.')
B.aoo=s(["guests","hospitality","guest rights"],t.s)
B.bnJ=new A.K(B.aoo,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest." (Sahih al-Bukhari 6018, Sahih Muslim 47). The sunnah of hospitality: welcome with a smile, offer the best food, do not ask when they will leave, and escort them to the door.')
B.aES=s(["backbiting","gossip","ghibah","slander"],t.s)
B.brU=new A.K(B.aES,'Allah says: "And do not spy or backbite each other. Would one of you like to eat the flesh of his brother when dead? You would detest it." (Qur\'an 49:12). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Backbiting is to mention your brother with what he dislikes." (Sahih Muslim 2589). Even if true, it is forbidden.')
B.aJC=s(["lying","truth","honesty"],t.s)
B.bpL=new A.K(B.aJC,"The Prophet \ufdfa taught that truthfulness leads to righteousness and righteousness to Paradise, while lying leads to wickedness and wickedness to the Fire (Sahih al-Bukhari 6094, Sahih Muslim 2607). He said that whoever reconciles people by saying good is not a liar; the narrator Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri added that he had not heard lying permitted except in three cases: war, reconciling people, and speech between husband and wife (Sahih Muslim 2605).")
B.aAr=s(["cheating","dishonesty","fraud","deception"],t.s)
B.brW=new A.K(B.aAr,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Whoever cheats us is not one of us." (Sahih Muslim 101). Cheating in business, exams, or relationships is forbidden. Allah says: "Woe to those who give less [than due], Who, when they take a measure from people, take in full, But if they give by measure or by weight to them, they cause loss." (Qur\'an 83:1-3).')
B.aO5=s(["forgiveness","forgive others","let go"],t.s)
B.boO=new A.K(B.aO5,'Allah says: "and let them pardon and overlook. Would you not like that Allah should forgive you?" (Qur\'an 24:22). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "The strong is not the one who overcomes people by his strength, but the strong is the one who controls himself while in anger." (Sahih al-Bukhari 6114, Sahih Muslim 2609).')
B.aNk=s(["gratitude","shukr","thankful","appreciation"],t.s)
B.bnV=new A.K(B.aNk,'Allah says: "If you are grateful, I will surely increase you." (Qur\'an 14:7). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Whoever is not grateful to people is not grateful to Allah." (Sunan Abi Dawud 4811, sahih per al-Albani). Gratitude is not just saying alhamdulillah \u2014 it is using blessings in obedience to Allah.')
B.aLU=s(["sabr","patience","endurance","perseverance"],t.s)
B.bns=new A.K(B.aLU,'Allah says: "Indeed, the patient will be given their reward without account." (Qur\'an 39:10). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Patience is at the first stroke of calamity." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1302, Sahih Muslim 926). There are three types: patience in obedience, patience against sin, and patience in affliction.')
B.aH_=s(["contentment","qanaah","satisfied","enough"],t.s)
B.bnk=new A.K(B.aH_,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Richness is not having many possessions. Rather, true richness is the richness of the soul." (Sahih al-Bukhari 6446, Sahih Muslim 1051). Contentment (qana\'ah) is a treasure that no one can steal.')
B.aHN=s(["humility","tawadu","modest","humble"],t.s)
B.bpM=new A.K(B.aHN,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Whoever humbles himself for Allah, Allah will raise him." (Sahih Muslim 2588). He was the most humble of people \u2014 he mended his own clothes, milked goats, and sat with the poor.')
B.aLv=s(["generosity","sakhaw","giving","charitable"],t.s)
B.brA=new A.K(B.aLv,"Generosity (sakha') is a mark of faith: it draws a person closer to Allah and to people, while miserliness does the opposite. Give what you can, even if it is small, and give sincerely.")
B.aFl=s(["courage","shajaah","brave","fearless"],t.s)
B.bp8=new A.K(B.aFl,'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "The strong believer is better and more beloved to Allah than the weak believer, while there is good in both." (Sahih Muslim 2664). Courage in Islam is not absence of fear \u2014 it is acting rightly despite fear.')
B.aD8=s(["wisdom","hikmah","understanding","insight"],t.s)
B.bos=new A.K(B.aD8,'Allah says: "He gives wisdom to whom He wills, and whoever has been given wisdom has certainly been given much good." (Qur\'an 2:269). Wisdom grows by learning, reflecting, and acting on what you know.')
B.aIN=s(["justice","adl","fairness","equity"],t.s)
B.bqK=new A.K(B.aIN,'Allah says: "Indeed, Allah commands you to render trusts to whom they are due and when you judge between people to judge with justice." (Qur\'an 4:58). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "The just will be with Allah on pulpits of light." (Sahih Muslim 1827).')
B.axw=s(["unity","ummah","muslim unity","brotherhood"],t.s)
B.boL=new A.K(B.axw,'Allah says: "And hold firmly to the rope of Allah all together and do not become divided." (Qur\'an 3:103). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "The believers in their mutual love, mercy, and compassion are like a single body." (Sahih al-Bukhari 6011, Sahih Muslim 2586).')
B.aAq=s(["dawah","inviting","calling to islam","share islam"],t.s)
B.bp9=new A.K(B.aAq,'Allah says: "Invite to the way of your Lord with wisdom and good instruction, and argue with them in a way that is best." (Qur\'an 16:125). The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Convey from me even if it is one verse." (Sahih al-Bukhari 3461).')
B.aIF=s(["jihad","struggle","striving"],t.s)
B.bqd=new A.K(B.aIF,"Allah says: \"And strive for Allah with the striving due to Him.\" (Qur'an 22:78). Jihad means striving. It includes striving against one's own desires, in worship and in good character, and speaking truth with wisdom and courage. Fighting, where it applies at all, has strict conditions set by qualified scholars and lawful authority: it is never for an individual to decide alone.")
B.aOt=s(["caliphate","khilafah","islamic state","political islam"],t.s)
B.boI=new A.K(B.aOt,"The first four caliphs (Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali) are known as the Rightly Guided Caliphs and are the model. Political engagement is part of Islam, but must be through legitimate means.")
B.ar2=s(["shariah","islamic law","fiqh","four schools","four madhabs","name the four schools","what are the four schools","what are the madhabs","names of the four schools"],t.s)
B.brs=new A.K(B.ar2,'Shariah is the divine law revealed by Allah. Fiqh is the human understanding and application of that law. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "The scholars are the heirs of the prophets." (Sunan Abi Dawud 3641, sahih per al-Albani). There are four major schools of fiqh: Hanafi, Maliki, Shafi\'i, and Hanbali.')
B.aB5=s(["fiqh schools","madhab","hanafi","maliki","shafii","hanbali","why do scholars disagree","why do scholars differ","why scholars differ","why scholars disagree","difference of opinion","differences of opinion","why are there different madhabs","why are there four schools"],t.s)
B.brw=new A.K(B.aB5,"The four schools are valid paths to the same truth. Differences between qualified scholars on questions open to ijtihad are recognised as legitimate, and Muslims are asked to be gentle with each other about them. A layperson should follow one school consistently under a qualified teacher.")
B.aO_=s(["ijtihad","scholarly reasoning","independent judgment"],t.s)
B.br2=new A.K(B.aO_,'Ijtihad is the effort to derive rulings from the Qur\'an and Sunnah. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "When a judge gives a ruling, striving to apply his reasoning, and is correct, he has two rewards. If he gives a ruling and errs, he has one reward." (Sahih al-Bukhari 7352, Sahih Muslim 1716).')
B.aKl=s(["qiyas","analogy","deductive reasoning"],t.s)
B.bp4=new A.K(B.aKl,"Qiyas is analogical reasoning: applying a known ruling to a new case based on a shared underlying cause ('illah). It is accepted by the majority of scholars as a source of Islamic law, provided the original ruling is from the Qur'an or authentic Sunnah.")
B.aCT=s(["ijma","consensus","scholarly agreement"],t.s)
B.bnR=new A.K(B.aCT,"Ijma is the consensus of the qualified scholars of the Ummah on a particular issue. Scholars treat it as a binding source of law after the Qur'an and the Sunnah.")
B.aDZ=s(["hadith sciences","isnad","matn","hadith authentication"],t.s)
B.bqw=new A.K(B.aDZ,"Hadith scholars built a science to protect the Prophet's words from error and invention. Hadith authentication examines: (1) the chain (isnad), (2) the text (matn), (3) the narrators' reliability. Classifications: sahih, hasan, da'if, mawdu'.")
B.aH0=s(["sahih","authentic hadith","sound hadith"],t.s)
B.bo4=new A.K(B.aH0,"Sahih is a hadith with a continuous chain of reliable narrators, free from defects, and not contradictory to stronger evidence. The most authentic collections are Sahih al-Bukhari and Sahih Muslim.")
B.aFw=s(["hasan","good hadith","fair hadith"],t.s)
B.boR=new A.K(B.aFw,"Hasan is a hadith with a continuous chain of narrators who are mostly reliable but may have slight weaknesses. It is accepted as evidence in Islamic law. The collections of Sunan al-Tirmidhi, Sunan Abi Dawud, Sunan al-Nasa'i, and Sunan Ibn Majah contain many hasan hadiths.")
B.aKM=s(["daif","weak hadith","unreliable hadith"],t.s)
B.bms=new A.K(B.aKM,"Da'if is a hadith with a chain containing a narrator who is weak (unreliable memory, unknown, or accused of lying). It cannot be used as independent evidence for rulings but may be used for virtues (fada'il) and encouragement (targhib).")
B.aDl=s(["mawdu","fabricated hadith","fake hadith"],t.s)
B.bn7=new A.K(B.aDl,'Mawdu is a fabricated hadith, invented and falsely attributed to the Prophet \ufdfa. It is a major sin to fabricate hadith. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his seat in the Fire." (Sahih al-Bukhari 106, Sahih Muslim 3).')
B.aIH=s(["zina","adultery","fornication","boyfriend","girlfriend","relationship before marriage","haram relationship","talking to a girl","talking to a boy"],t.s)
B.bmA=new A.K(B.aIH,"Allah says: \u201cAnd do not approach unlawful sexual intercourse. Indeed, it is ever an immorality and is evil as a way.\u201d (Qur\u2019an 17:32). The verse says do not even APPROACH it \u2014 so the early steps matter, not only the last one. And for whatever has already happened, the door of return is open: \u201cDo not despair of the mercy of Allah \u2014 indeed, Allah forgives all sins.\u201d (Qur\u2019an 39:53). For your specific situation, a trusted local scholar can walk with you privately.")
B.aI3=s(["allah hates me","allah hate me","allah doesnt love me","allah does not love me","allah dont love me","allah is angry with me","allah is punishing me","allah abandoned me","allah has abandoned me","allah left me","allah forgot me","allah wont forgive me","allah will not forgive me","allah cant forgive me"],t.s)
B.bqg=new A.K(B.aI3,"I am glad you said that out loud. Hear this first: Allah says, \u201cYour Lord has not taken leave of you, [O Muhammad], nor has He detested [you].\u201d (Qur'an 93:3). That was revealed to the Prophet \ufdfa himself during a pause in the revelation. And to the one weighed down by sins: \u201cSay, O My servants who have transgressed against themselves [by sinning], do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins.\u201d (Qur'an 39:53). A heart that fears it has lost Allah is still turned toward Him. Sakina is the quiet page of this app, and For Your Heart can help you find words for what you feel. I am listening if you want to tell me more.\n[GO:/sakina]\n[GO:/feelings]")
B.aJ_=s(["old to pray","kid to pray","kids to pray","child to pray","children to pray","son to pray","daughter to pray","teach children","teach kids","teach my child","teach my son","teach my daughter","doesnt want to pray","does not want to pray","refuses to pray","wont pray","children and prayer"],t.s)
B.bq5=new A.K(B.aJ_,"Children learn prayer from love and from watching you. The Prophet \ufdfa said to command children to pray when they are seven and to discipline them over it when they are ten (Sunan Abi Dawud 495, hasan sahih per al-Albani). Begin gently: let them stand beside you, praise every small step, and keep it short. If a child pushes back, stay patient and keep praying in front of them, and make du'a for them. Allah says: \u201cAnd enjoin prayer upon your family [and people] and be steadfast therein.\u201d (Qur'an 20:132). For a child who is struggling, a teacher at your masjid can help. The Wasia Academy is made for learning step by step.\n[GO:/academy]")
B.aAH=s(["meaning of surah ikhlas","what does surah ikhlas mean","meaning of ikhlas","what does ikhlas mean","meaning of al ikhlas"],t.s)
B.boF=new A.K(B.aAH,"Surah al-Ikhlas (112) is four verses on the oneness of Allah: \u201cSay, He is Allah, [who is] One, Allah, the Eternal Refuge. He neither begets nor is born, nor is there to Him any equivalent.\u201d (Qur'an 112:1-4). The word ikhlas means pure sincerity: giving Allah what is His alone.")
